{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs","id":1536991,"title":"Sabbat as nuanced player characters vs. murder hobo NPCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-08T10:15:08-07:00","id":1536991,"title":"Sabbat as nuanced player characters vs. murder hobo NPCs","content":"There's a problem with the Sabbat that is basically summarized by me as &quot;The Doctor Doom Paradox&quot; which is like the Magneto Paradox but they've more or less settled on him. The Doctor Doom Paradox is that every ten years or so, someone decides to either redeem Doctor Doom. He starts acting like a hero or doing heroic things that highlights that maybe he's not as bad as all that. The problem being that Doctor Doom is one of the most popular and well-liked villains of all of the setting so then someone else comes out with something that has Doctor Doom do something absolutely horrible that resets it to the status quo.<br /> <br /> Fans like the Sabbat being expanded on as being a much more nuanced 3-dimensional antagonist by 2nd Edition until many people were playing them more than the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> But the Sabbat exist to be the murder hobos who get shot in the face as their role in the game. They exist because there's a long history of vampires who are just murderous thugs and idiot hell raisers like NEAR DARK and plenty of other stories where vampires are just complete monsters. Part of the conception of the Sabbat was the idea that they're dominated by the Beast and this is a Bad ThingTM. They never &quot;stopped&quot; being guys who played football with human heads (and that's soccer not American football, you damn Yanks) but they got the nicest shade put on them by the Paths of Enlightenment--which were themselves just meant to be in-universe the &quot;Path of whatever the Regent wants you to do.&quot; You need the contrast to the Camarilla and Anarchs of vampires who have just lost everything and become utter monsters.<br /> <br /> However, a major allure of V:TM in the first place was playing &quot;the Bad GuyTM.&quot; It was an appeal in the 90s when it first started that you wouldn't be a Lawful Good wandering murderer ala D&amp;D or Call of Cthulhu investigator bound to get eaten. No, you would be a monster struggling wiht their humanity and while some of you would be Angel or Hannibal King, a lot of you would still fall prey to the Beast. So the whole argument the Sabbat should be off-limits doesn't really hold water. It's the same reason playing a Giovanni or Setite is viable even though both of them are every bit as vile as the Sword of Caine.<br /> <br /> I think it really boils down to whether you think the Paths/Roads are viable or not. Justin Achilli made them utter nonsense in Revised and basically, most Paths are just vamprires brainwashing themselves into thinking they're being enlightened when it's just a temporary bandaid against the Beast. That most Sabbat are just Low Humanity. This is a direct contrast against the Dark Ages, though, where Roads are as common as Humanity (and Humanity is just another Road) and a perfectly valid means of Kindred expression. They also had redeeming qualities so no Road was just, &quot;I'm an evil bastard. Get with it.&quot; Even the Road of the Devil was like, &quot;God sucks, let's overthrow him for the good of all.&quot;<br /> <br /> So what do you think? The Sabbat could use some nuance but I also feel like they really should be a failed alternative to the Anarchs. Once you succumb to the Beast, you really can't come back from it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:04:58-07:00","id":1536995,"title":"","content":"I never cared for the path of enlightenment themes at all and avoided it and that was one of the big things I liked about VTR is they did away with that concept.<br /> <br /> I was more into DC myself, but I would see how both Doom and Magneto would go through periods of being heroic and outright villiany.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:15:31-07:00","id":1536997,"title":"","content":"It feels really quite strange to me that the designated antagonist Sect would include more playable factions and templates than the Sect that's supposed to be the focus of the line. I can't exactly fault any player for preferring the schizophrenic smorgasbord that is the Sabbat when the game itself appears to say you must align yourself with the Sect if you want to pursue any plotline or character archetype more exotic than doing Dracula re-enactments of <i>The Godfather</i>. I'm not saying this is a <i>good</i> thing\u2014some of the Sabbat's internal diversity seems frankly incomprehensible to me. Why would the Lilith-worshipping Bahari align themselves with the Sword of Caine? What is stopping a Kiasyd from joining the Camarilla? Why on Earth is the Camarilla suddenly intent on persecuting Noddists?<br /> <br /> There's not much I like about V5, but I think they were right to distance themselves from the very concept of &quot;Sect politics&quot; and shatter the Sabbat into more than one Cult (cf. the Church of Caine). I truly believe there's no need for a designated antagonist faction in V:tM\u2014playing the antagonist <i>is</i> the central appeal of the game, as you say\u2014but I do think it's always good to have a rich selection of conspiracies-within-conspiracies to sow paranoia among the players. I still wish V5 committed to the version being a reboot from the very beginning, though. I don't think there was any way to return spice to the two primary factions while maintaining continuity with previous versions of the game; too much had already been drained out of the Camarilla and the Anarchs for any deconstruction of the Sabbat to not come across as a personal attack on those players who prefer the Sword of Caine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:55:25-07:00","id":1537024,"title":"","content":"My main problem with a murder hobo Sabbat is that I can't suspend my disbelief enough to see it working as a social construct like a sect. A bunch of almost-Wights can not function as an efficient group, and frankly even the more nuanced and revised version of it stretches the band-aids of Vinculum and Paths to their limits.<br /> This has led to the Sabbat's eeeevilness becoming much toned down in my games, because a) some of it is so stupid it is self-destructive and b) it doesn't need it to be a counterpart to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I honestly prefer to have them as a dogmatic but different group vis-a-vis the Anarchs and Camarilla, together with the independents they form something of a Mario, Luigi, Wario, and Waluigi constellation that works well as a closed system. So in summary I like the Sabbat as 'the other bad guys' rather than 'the bad bad guys'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T13:34:12-07:00","id":1537027,"title":"","content":"The original Sabbat had a lot more variety to them. Revised did its best to nuke any kind of diversity within the Sabbat so that everyone was now essentially a member of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> I believe the original purpose of the Sabbat in the setting was to provide a way to portray pre-Anne Rice vampires: the kind of vampires that show up, turn whomever they bite into more vampires, worship Satan (at least in the Hammer movies), and be villainous as opposed to the more nuanced portrayal of vampires in the Camarilla and Anarchs. However, the initial Sabbat sourcebooks provided a lot of diversity within that framework. Here are some examples<br /> <br /> First, there were large numbers of Country Gangrel who were on the Path of Harmony, and they seemed to be one of those aspects of the Sabbat that existed pre-revised Code of Milan before the Sabbat became more centralized.<br /> <br /> Second, the Loyalist movement seemed to have a lot of Cainites who objected to the more monstrous Sabbat. I think that is why the character of Dominique was included in Children of the Inquisition. She was there to show there was a powerful movement within the Sabbat that objected. Yet now she's the forgotten character of CotI even though everyone else became a well known NPC.<br /> <br /> Third, many nomad packs - heavily influenced by the Country Gangrel and Loyalists - had a wide variety of vampire types. They were often on their own, and therefore didn't participate that often in the more gruesome ritae like founded covens often did.<br /> <br /> Fourth, there were groups who were not portrayed as that much different from their Camarilla counterparts. Yeah, the Malkavian and Toreador antitribu were darker, but the Brujah antitribu did not seem all that different. The Ventrue antitribu were mostly hard core loyalists and seemed to be the &quot;conscience&quot; of the sect. and the Nosferatu antitribu were basically the same as Nosferatu except they were hedging their bets. They would even met the other Nosferatu under truce and exchange information!<br /> <br /> Fifth, we would later learn that much of the Black Hand's leadership, the supposed sword of caine, was in fact part of an enemy sect who were appalled at how the Sabbat treated humanity and working to destroy the sect from within.<br /> <br /> Sixth, all of this was possible because of the central tension of a sect based on absolute freedom versus the need for the sect to survive against its enemies. The murder hobo aspect was certainly a big part of the sect, but it was not intended to be the only part of the sect. If not for the metaplot of Revised, this would have been kept in future sourcebooks. But since it made impossible how Justin Achilli wanted the metaplot to be, he just ignored everything that got in his way and included a lot of &quot;yeah, those guys are all gone&quot; comments in Revised's Guide to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> The major flaw of many Paths of Enlightenment is that the writers forgot the purpose of any Path (including the Path of Humanity) is to BIND the Beast so that it does not overwhelm the vampire and hijack control. Which means that any successful, well developed Path must somehow control the Beast and therefore deny its ability to take over. That meant telling the Beast &quot;no&quot; whenever it was hungry, afraid, or indulged too much. That could be based on simply coming up with reason to say &quot;no&quot; (based on Conviction or Self-Control), or allowing it some measure of satiety (Instinct) so that it was appeased and would not try to take over. Too many Paths of Enlightenment, while providing some measure of internal consistency, did not seem based around denying the Beast which is why they were derided as &quot;Paths of Doing Anything I Want&quot;. Fundamentally, if the Path was not somehow constraining/denying the Beast, it could not be a successful Path as eventually the vampire could fall to the Beast and become a wight.<br /> <br /> While some Paths were developed well enough in that aspect, others were not. So it's not surprising future writers and many players forgot what was supposed to be the purpose of any Path.<br /> <br /> I think one thing that might have been interesting in the setting is to have Sabbat remember various &quot;failed Paths&quot; that didn't work as intended, and therefore abandoned as mistakes. And perhaps certain NPCs working to refine some of these failed Paths into a coherent, systemic philosophy that could do what the Sabbat needed them to do which is prevent vampires from becoming wights. You could even have in Sabbat chronicles the idea that sometimes entire packs become wights because they didn't take their Path seriously, and rest of the local sect needs to wipe them out. It should be an ongoing problem in the sect.<br /> <br /> If you have a Sabbat chronicle where the failure of members to adequately take their Paths seriously lead to problems with wights, then there definitely is a role for more &quot;humane&quot;, nuanced PCs and NPCs instead of them seeming like anomalies. &quot;Say what you will about the Path of Harmony, the Country Gangrel don't have a lot of wights amongst them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":11},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T18:44:36-07:00","id":1537049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs#post1536991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also feel like they really should be a failed alternative to the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Anarchs are boring. The Anarchs have always been the most boring sect. And any attempt to sacrifice the other sects on the alter of the Anarchs is inherently doomed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T19:06:11-07:00","id":1537050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537049#post1537049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. The Anarchs are boring. The Anarchs have always been the most boring sect. And any attempt to sacrifice the other sects on the alter of the Anarchs is inherently doomed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Sabbat are just warmed over Anarchs.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ooo, we hate the Camarilla and Traditions. We're all about freedom.&quot;<br /> <br /> Get your own thing, poseurs.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat aren't anything BUT Anarchs with Catholicism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T20:04:39-07:00","id":1537054,"title":"","content":"I always played the Sabbat as more nuanced characters, both as a player and as a storyteller. I feel like playing them as murderhobos is inherently a bad rp choice. But if that\u2019s what works best for your Chronicle, that\u2019s fine too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T01:28:53-07:00","id":1537065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537050#post1537050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the Sabbat are just warmed over Anarchs.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ooo, we hate the Camarilla and Traditions. We're all about freedom.&quot;<br /> <br /> Get your own thing, poseurs.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat aren't anything BUT Anarchs with Catholicism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah the anarchs are just diet carmarilla. The sabbat have distinct ideas and philisophical praxis even if we consider them a failure they're the most distinct of the sects. Alternate laws philosophy, clans, culture and internal organisation backed up with a clear write up on how they interact with the other sects and each other.<br /> <br /> this is not the say the anarchs are intrisically inferior more that sabbat has historically been better written. <br /> <br /> On reflection its telling that edgelords/ combat types were drawn to the sabbat when at a glance the anarch should have theoretically been the obvious choice for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T03:55:09-07:00","id":1537068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs#post1536991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a problem with the Sabbat that is basically summarized by me as &quot;The Doctor Doom Paradox&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there isn't.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat is a nuanced and diverse sect since its inception and through all editions but Revised.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Rumors</b></i> about the Sabbat say they're just almost wights murder hobos. But that's all we have in the core books, rumors, rumors that are obviously false in their over simplification.<br /> <br /> If you want to use Anarchy, use Anarchs. If you want to use low Humanity vampires or Wights, use them. The game has those options already without the Sabbat. It exists to be its own thing, in fact a lot of other things, but if you can't see it, just drop the Sabbat from your games and use actual murder hobos, you'll be better served.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T04:12:46-07:00","id":1537070,"title":"","content":"Out of left field take, but if you want a more nuanced take on the Sabbat, I suggest the Kuei-Jin, specifically the non-heretical dharmas.<br /> <br /> They don't pine for their humanity, they accept themselves as monsters, but they are monsters with a righteous purpose. They have spiritual aspects to their existence, but they tend to focus on what is happening in the mortal world. The Dharmas just give a specific spin on what the details of that are to the individual Kuei-Jin.<br /> <br /> This isn't surprising how the Kindred of the East books were made much later in the development cycle than most of the vampire stuff, thus the ideas and concepts had matured and been refined over time.<br /> <br /> KotE basically flips most of VtM on its head by saying their version of the Sabbat with each dharma being a Path of Enlightenment and clan in one, is the only game in town and they are the &quot;good guys&quot; that protect the world even as their actions corrupt and harm it. The few dharmas that embrace subservient spirituality or embrace humanity are considered heretical and dangerous. The bad guys of the setting aren't ancient vampires, but the demon lords who corrupt ancient vampires as a way to pass the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T05:26:45-07:00","id":1537077,"title":"","content":"On reflection while I dislike reductive cliches abou tvtm like &quot;the Sabbat is the dark mirror of the camarilla&quot; or &quot;the sabbat is a medieval death cult.&quot; their is something to this comparison to the doom comparison. Doom character develops beyond his initial boundaries and then is forced to snap back due to editorial mandate. This is effectively what happened with v5 Sabbat/ the game had moved way beyond the early belials brood style sabbat but someone somewhere didn't like that ida so tried to push them back in a tiny box.<br /> It's a worrying implication of how the game is developing that they're now latching on to comic style writing, which have a trend towards stagnancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T07:04:26-07:00","id":1537080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537065#post1537065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah the anarchs are just diet carmarilla. The sabbat have distinct ideas and philisophical praxis even if we consider them a failure they're the most distinct of the sects. Alternate laws philosophy, clans, culture and internal organisation backed up with a clear write up on how they interact with the other sects and each other.<br /> <br /> this is not the say the anarchs are intrisically inferior more that sabbat has historically been better written.<br /> <br /> On reflection its telling that edgelords/ combat types were drawn to the sabbat when at a glance the anarch should have theoretically been the obvious choice for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This. The Anarchs definitely suffered from being the awkward middle child of the main sects. The Camarilla had all the power and structure, and the Sabbat were given all the freedom. The Anarchs existed somewhere in the middle, which made them stand out less. If players wanted to operate in Kindred politics, they stuck with the Camarilla. Whereas if they wanted to do whatever they wanted, they went for the Sabbat (which did everything the Anarchs claimed to do, but better).<br /> <br /> What's worse, the writers seemed intent on funneling all the most interesting ideas exclusively into the Sabbat (or into the independent Clans or Bloodlines, as the case may be). The Anarchs were the neglected sect, not given the right kind of write-ups that would make them appealing to run.<br /> <br /> That the Camarilla and Sabbat were the main belligerents in the regular crusades between territories didn't help. There's a lot more fun adventures to be had engaging in that conflict, than in awkwardly standing to the side. Often enough, because Anarchs were treated as the &quot;loyal opposition&quot; to the Camarilla, they ended up fighting on the Camarilla's side in such wars anyway.<br /> <br /> It's weird that more focus wasn't centered around attempts by Anarchs to establish their own power structures (or lack thereof). The various counter-cultural movements from mortals, reflected in their undead counterparts.<br /> <br /> Granted, Anarchs on their own tended to miss the main conflict point the Anarchs were designed to embody: the youth agitating against the entrenched power structures of the old. Before the Sabbat entered the picture in a real way, VtM was all about this dynamic. (I would argue one of the failings of V5 was the use of the Beckoning to remove Elders en masse, thereby robbing the game of a defined antagonist to butt heads with. Which is why V5 went on to walk back the Beckoning, because Paradox wants to have its cake and eat it too. But I digress.). What do you do with a sect (pseudo-sect?) that is written primarily to be in opposition to its &quot;parent&quot; sect, when that &quot;parent&quot; isn't around?<br /> <br /> I mean, that's what the writers should have been doing. Finding ways to make the Anarchs compelling, in their own way. If all they have going for them is being rebels, well...the Sabbat arguably enable the player characters to rebel HARDER. (Provided you don't mind being manipulated by your own old monsters. Really, the Anarchs needed to have it underscored how false the dichotomy between the Camarilla and Sabbat were, to show how the Anarchs were the one true sect of independence. The other two were Controlled Opposition.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T12:47:31-07:00","id":1537100,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat were one of the best aspects of VTM and hands down one the best foils against the Camarilla, leagues ahead of what they tried to do with the Anarchs. Nothing else comes even close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:32:56-07:00","id":1537112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537080#post1537080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^This. The Anarchs definitely suffered from being the awkward middle child of the main sects. The Camarilla had all the power and structure, and the Sabbat were given all the freedom. The Anarchs existed somewhere in the middle, which made them stand out less. If players wanted to operate in Kindred politics, they stuck with the Camarilla. Whereas if they wanted to do whatever they wanted, they went for the Sabbat (which did everything the Anarchs claimed to do, but better).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue something different. I've known lots of players who loved playing Sabbat. The thing that attracted them was not &quot;freedom&quot; or &quot;to do whatever they wanted&quot;. It was the distinctive element of Sabbat culture and organization. They loved the idea of Paths of Enlightenment. They liked the various ritae. They liked the distinction between nomads packs and founded coven. They liked the intrigues among the Bishops and Archbishops. They liked the tension between the ducti and priests. They liked that monomacy and diablerie were acceptable. They liked the idea of the Caitiff joining together as the Panders and forcing the clans to take them seriously. They liked the mythology of defeating the antedeluvians and Noddist lore. They liked the internal tension created by the Sabbat Inquisition and the Black Hand within the sect. Certainly some preferred playing Loyalists and leaned into the Sabbat's freedom line, but even those players knew the sect overall was clamping down on that. What they liked was reacting against that structure while still participating in it.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Sabbat provided a strong framework for PCs to roleplay in. The unique institutions and culture of the Sabbat inspired their creativity despite being a constraint on what they could ultimately do because it provided lots of tools they could use to customize their characters and chronicles. People who liked the Camarilla likewise liked the Camarilla because of its unique institutions and culture. Both sects provided lots of tools to players to craft interesting characters and insert them into fun situations.<br /> <br /> What made the Anarchs less appealing was not that they existed &quot;somewhere in the middle&quot;. It was they lacked any kind of interesting framework or organization that made them stand out. The Anarchs, in contrast to the Camarilla and Sabbat, seemed bland. There wasn't enough hooks and distinctive elements that could cause players to easily create distinctive characters. Everyone just seemed like a generic thug. The Anarchs, as a group, lacked the kind of tools that both the Camarilla and Sabbat provided. All the Anarchs were, were vampires who opposed the Prince the most, and that was about it. Other than that, there wasn't much that was distinctive about them.<br /> <br /> Now very early in the game, it didn't seem like that. Chicago By Night provided us several different groups of Anarchs that seemed to indicate there were ideological, political, or personality divides among the Anarchs. The Brujah clanbook and other sourcebooks mentioned an Anarch Council that seemed to be running the revolution. The Anarch Cookbook provided some key personalities and political testaments. This built up a lot of enthusiasm and expectation that the upcoming sourcebook Los Angeles By Night was going to be a big sourcebook with lots of interesting lore. Instead, what people actually got was disappointing to a lot of players. It sucked a lot of energy out of players for Anarchs, and I remember at the time seeing players who had played mostly Anarchs previously just no longer be interested in the sect and changing their play styles. Because as the Player Guides and clanbooks came out, the culture and offices of the Camarilla made it seem more fun to play in.<br /> <br /> I think if Los Angeles By Night or some other sourcebook had provided more structure, factions, and ideas about the Anarchs, then they would have kept a lot of their initial popularity. The Anarchs simply didn't have the cool toys or tools that the other groups did.<br /> <br /> I do think it was possible to have provided the Anarchs with those kind of tools. I brainstormed some of them back in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them/page5\">this thread, starting around tab 5</a>. Create some large scale political factions among the Anarchs (and their internal rivalries and feuds). Make it clear the Anarchs are not limited to those, and many of those factions are internally split, but having them would help players create new characters. Provide some real detail on the Anarch Council and how it has actual loyal operatives in other domains. Many Anarchs may not be affiliated with it, but making it a Comintern like structure that does provide some help and guidance, a network of support, and various assets is another good tool for players and STs. Also provide the obvious counterpart to that - describe how the Anarchs are riddled with informers, double agents, cowards, and how the Camarilla in general and Justicar Petrodon in particular undermine and combat them. Describe their relations with the Sabbat, particularly between them and Sabbat Loyalists and what they have in common and what divides them. Are they just enemies, do some Sabbat Loyalists actually prefer the Anarchs to their recently centralizing sect, is their Sabbat brainwashing too much for them to do so? All of these would provide lots of tools that could cause players to latch onto the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> But the Anarchs never got any cool toys that only they got to play with.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T17:15:14-07:00","id":1537123,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat are for players that want to be chaotic-evil murder-hobos. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1536995#post1536995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never cared for the path of enlightenment themes at all and avoided it and that was one of the big things I liked about VTR is they did away with that concept.<br /> <br /> I was more into DC myself, but I would see how both Doom and Magneto would go through periods of being heroic and outright villiany.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never cared for the Roads and when running Dark Ages, I only had Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":12},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T19:11:07-07:00","id":1537126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537123#post1537123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat are for players that want to be chaotic-evil murder-hobos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's a bit more to the Sabbat than just being Chaotic-Evil. Like a Ventrue Antitribu on the Path of Honor is likely going to be more Lawful-Evil than Chaotic-Evil. Every Sabbat is going to be evil though, murder, especially murder of regular people, is a pretty major point of their organization. And they're not necessarily hobos, they have their own cities and areas they control.<br /> <br /> Though note that's for older editions. In V5 they absolutely only are chaotic-evil murder-hobos.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T20:45:16-07:00","id":1537130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537126#post1537126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there's a bit more to the Sabbat than just being Chaotic-Evil. Like a Ventrue Antitribu on the Path of Honor is likely going to be more Lawful-Evil than Chaotic-Evil. Every Sabbat is going to be evil though, murder, especially murder of regular people, is a pretty major point of their organization. And they're not necessarily hobos, they have their own cities and areas they control.<br /> <br /> Though note that's for older editions. In V5 they absolutely only are chaotic-evil murder-hobos.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, it's slightly more complicated than that. All of the Sabbat Elders are bunkered down for Gehenna like Bezos and Zuckerberg while sending out the Sabbat as a massive cannon fodder army of Zerg while they bark orders via radio or telepathy.<br /> <br /> At least according to Justin Achilli.<br /> <br /> Which is still far far less interesting than the Old Sabbat and I had my criticisms of the Old Sabbat (The Sabbat's handling is what finally killed my faith in V5)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T23:01:41-07:00","id":1537132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-pl