bat as a massive cannon fodder army of Zerg while they bark orders via radio or telepathy.<br /> <br /> At least according to Justin Achilli.<br /> <br /> Which is still far far less interesting than the Old Sabbat and I had my criticisms of the Old Sabbat (The Sabbat's handling is what finally killed my faith in V5)</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the impression the actual sabbat/elders hiding in a shed somewhere was more a write around to avoid acknowlaging how absurd v5 sabbat were written and those guys are never going to make an appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T04:45:41-07:00","id":1537146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537134#post1537134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the impression the actual sabbat/elders hiding in a shed somewhere was more a write around to avoid acknowlaging how absurd v5 sabbat were written and those guys are never going to make an appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, while I love shitting on the Sabbat, the &quot;Angel of Caine&quot; opening (implied to be Vykos) more or less says this is the case doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T08:05:30-07:00","id":1537152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537130#post1537130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apparently, it's slightly more complicated than that. All of the Sabbat Elders are bunkered down for Gehenna like Bezos and Zuckerberg while sending out the Sabbat as a massive cannon fodder army of Zerg while they bark orders via radio or telepathy.<br /> <br /> At least according to Justin Achilli.<br /> <br /> Which is still far far less interesting than the Old Sabbat and I had my criticisms of the Old Sabbat (The Sabbat's handling is what finally killed my faith in V5)</div> </div> </div> </div>For real? Ugh, that is just... it's just painfully dumb. Like wow. I'm just sitting here shaking my head. I didn't like what they did with the Sabbat in V5, but it made a certain amount of sense.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat's leaders have always been hypocrites. They talk about brotherhood and equality, but they hoard all the money, all the power, all the blood and then send their pawns off to die. They're assholes, just like the leaders of pretty much all of the groups in the World of Darkness are assholes in some way. That's just the &quot;punk&quot; part of the setting's DNA. And it makes sense - the Sabbat grew out of the Anarch Rebellion. Of course many of the early Anarchs were mad about the way they were treated by elders, but a lot of them joined in because they wanted the power, influence and prestige held by the feudalistic elders and didn't want to wait hundreds or thousands of years. The Anarchs who went on to found the Sabbat did so with the idea that, &quot;We'll make our own sect with blackjack and hookers and I'll have all the power there that I would have been denied in the Camarilla.&quot; <br /> <br /> So the elders in the Sabbat had the power. Then they fed their offspring and their offspring's offspring stories all about the big war, the crusade, that they were brothers and they needed to go fight and die. This worked great until the Beckoning happened. Suddenly all of the Sabbat's elders vanished, and there was a huge power vacuum and you had a bunch of younger vampires step up to take over. Unlike the old hypocritical Sabbat leaders who had had come out of the Anarch Revolt, the new Sabbat leaders had been Embraced into the sect. They were the true believers. They believed in all of the stuff that the old hypocritical leaders refused to do. They tore the sect apart, drove out everyone who wasn't ideologically pure enough (like followers of various Paths or the way the Lasombra saw what was coming and left), and then burned everything that was left to the ground to devote themselves to the cause. <br /> <br /> This was a very obvious, kind of hamfisted parallel to conservativism in the US and other countries. In the US, many conservatives had publicly held views on things like shutting down the government, or banning abortion, but they never took steps to actually do those things. They were talking points to rally people, but the politicians knew how dangerous that stuff would be. But as they stepped down, they were replaced by people who had been born and raised on those talking points, and they thought that was stuff that they should be doing and suddenly you have a situation where the crazy people, who were not originally intended to be in charge, are in charge. It's not just a US thing, you're seeing it in Canada and Europe. <br /> <br /> Again, I didn't like what V5 did with the Sabbat, but I understood where it was coming from, it made a certain amount of logical sense within the setting, and it's easy to draw parallels to events in the modern day.<br /> <br /> But I guess now the Elders never actually vanished, they're just pulling the strings and burnt out their own sect and destroyed their entire powerbase, which they had spent centuries creating. It just feels pretty hollow and kind of stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T08:47:04-07:00","id":1537153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537146#post1537146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhh, while I love shitting on the Sabbat, the &quot;Angel of Caine&quot; opening (implied to be Vykos) more or less says this is the case doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but thats the same as the sabbat fighting the gehenna war in narnia. Theyre never getting involved or interacting in any meaningful context","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T13:38:25-07:00","id":1537159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537153#post1537153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but thats the same as the sabbat fighting the gehenna war in narnia. Theyre never getting involved or interacting in any meaningful context</div> </div> </div> </div>I was immediately reminded of Poochie from the Simpsons: &quot; 'I have to go now. My planet needs me', Note, Poochie died on the way back to his home planet.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T11:02:30-07:00","id":1537268,"title":"","content":"Elder Sabbat &quot; We are going to march into Camarilla domain and wipe them out, but we have prior engagements and won't be joining you on the front lines.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T16:29:46-07:00","id":1537435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537268#post1537268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elder Sabbat &quot; We are going to march into Camarilla domain and wipe them out, but we have prior engagements and won't be joining you on the front lines.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, &quot;Some of you may die, but that is a sacrifice I am willing to make,&quot; is pretty spot for most Sabbat elders. However, &quot;I'm going to burn down my powerbase, destroy my sect, wreck my domains and leave myself as lord of a burnt out ruin,&quot; isn't. I just can't see how the V5 Sabbat metaplot could have happened if the Sabbat Elders are actually still on the scene and pulling strings. It can only begin to make sense if they're not around anymore and the new leaders of the sect are all crazy psycho fanatics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T16:41:57-07:00","id":1537437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537435#post1537435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, &quot;Some of you may die, but that is a sacrifice I am willing to make,&quot; is pretty spot for most Sabbat elders. However, &quot;I'm going to burn down my powerbase, destroy my sect, wreck my domains and leave myself as lord of a burnt out ruin,&quot; isn't. I just can't see how the V5 Sabbat metaplot could have happened if the Sabbat Elders are actually still on the scene and pulling strings. It can only begin to make sense if they're not around anymore and the new leaders of the sect are all crazy psycho fanatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have of a lot of interesting stories and ideas for how to do the V5 Sabbat but it occurs to me that Paradox was never interested in explaining it so why should I have spent so much time thinking through.<br /> <br /> I am, however, interested in the Storyteller's Vault SABBAT: SCHISMS that's coming out at the end of the month. The premise for that being the Sabbat is actually split in two with the Gehenna Crusaders being essentially the mobile army of crazy people.<br /> <br /> I think the reason the Sabbat abandoned all of their territory was the Out of Universe reason that they didn't want huge chunks of the Central and South American player base to be denied Camarilla games in their hometowns. Not getting, I suspect, that most people worked around that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T17:01:42-07:00","id":1537441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537437#post1537437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not getting, I suspect, that most people worked around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's not like people haven't been retconning their hometowns since forever. In canon, New Orleans is Cammy. I'm a Cajun who runs Sabbat games, so New Orleans is Sabbat in my world.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T17:11:11-07:00","id":1537443,"title":"","content":"To complain some more about V5's Sabbat, it's also weird because the story is so convoluted and weird in its handling of things. It was clear they didn't know what they wanted to do with the Sabbat so they kept making weird uses for them like, &quot;They all went to the Middle East to fight Vampire Gods.&quot;<br /> <br /> They could have had:<br /> <br /> * A devastating civil war<br /> <br /> * They could have been the chief victims of the Second Inquisition due to their disregard for the Masquerade<br /> <br /> * They could have split into multiple sects and blood cults<br /> <br /> There's only a couple of hundred thousand vampires in the world even in the most overbloated estimation of vampire numbers so it's not like you had to do much to write away the Sabbat as a less prevalent part of the setting. Even if you didn't want them to be as prominent, you could just dial them down without destroying them completely or changing them utterly.<br /> <br /> I remember when Chicago by Night was a few years away from release that I had the Lasombra become a Camarilla clan because of the spoilers and my players asked, &quot;How did that work.&quot;<br /> <br /> I said, &quot;Well, the Lasombra Anttribu embraced a lot more and the Sabbat Lasombra had their numbers reduced by infighting so its now a more even mix. The former are now able to assert clan status and the latter can't wage effective war on their kinsmen. Maybe like a hundred defected.&quot;<br /> <br /> There, done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T19:56:29-07:00","id":1537456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537443#post1537443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To complain some more about V5's Sabbat, it's also weird because the story is so convoluted and weird in its handling of things. It was clear they didn't know what they wanted to do with the Sabbat so they kept making weird uses for them like, &quot;They all went to the Middle East to fight Vampire Gods.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I wouldn't even necessarily mind that. The Beckoning is supposed to be a big thing, most of the Elders have gone to the Middle East both the Camarilla's Elders and (in theory) the Sabbat's Elders, and it would make sense that more Sabbat members would head over there than Camarilla members. Many would get dragged along because of their vinculum ties, or simply because killing Elder vampires in the Gehenna Crusade is kind of a big thing that the Sabbat does. It's not hard to imagine that a lot of them would say, &quot;Gehenna is here! Our time has come!&quot; and head off to fight. Personally I intensely dislike the idea of the Beckoning, but this is stuff that makes sense given the context of V5.<br /> <br /> But then the books never did anything else with the Beckoning, due to the fact that it's such a massive world-shaking piece of metaplot that any sort of examination of it is going to take the focus off of the street-level stories that V5 wants players to prioritize. And then apparently Justin is suggesting that the Sabbat elders weren't really affected by the Beckoning and didn't join in the Gehenna War. They're actually still around, and still in charge of the Sabbat, it's just that they decided to implode their own sect and destroy everything they've spent centuries building for reasons - even though the Beckoning and Gehenna War are a pretty solid explanation as to why Sabbat Elders wouldn't be around why the sect would collapse without them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T20:51:08-07:00","id":1537458,"title":"","content":"I didn't have the Sabbat remotely implode in my games, but I DID have them lose some cities. In my games, the reason for this is that the Cathari started to dominate the sect after the canon stuff with the Regent happened. The Cathari started becoming extremely bloated by raising any shovelhead to True Sabbat status once they displayed clear loyalty to the Path of Cathari. Consequently the Cathari became, by far, the largest Path in the Sabbat. This lead to the rise of the Cathari Demagogues to leadership of the Sabbat. These Cathari demagogues and their masses of shovelhead-in-all-but-name followers were more interested in hedonism than good governance, so the Sabbat as a whole became loud and sloppy, even in their home cities.<br /> <br /> This caused the loss of several important cities. The Cathari leaders started spewing out absurd propaganda about how &quot;the Sabbat doesn't need our own cities&quot; and &quot;we are more dangerous than ever without our own cities.&quot;<br /> <br /> This propaganda was so ridiculous that it united the leaders of the other Paths against the Cathari. The Grand Inquisitor lead a siege on New Orleans, and made it the new capital of the Sabbat once they conquered it. The Sabbat Inquisition declared the Regent position abolished, declared the Cathari path heretical, and declared that the Sabbat Inquisition was taking control over the sect.<br /> <br /> The Grand Inquisitor is now the leader of the Sabbat in my games. Or more precisely, she becomes the leader of the Sabbat again and again every time I restart my Siege of New Orleans campaign.<br /> <br /> One day I really need to do a sequel to the Siege of New Orleans campaign, and explore the long term consequences of the Grand Inquisitor position replacing the Regent as the top Sabbat position. But so far I've mostly just completed the campaign, taken a rest for a while, refined the campaign's design, and then restarted it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T20:56:45-07:00","id":1537460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537456#post1537456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, I wouldn't even necessarily mind that. The Beckoning is supposed to be a big thing, most of the Elders have gone to the Middle East both the Camarilla's Elders and (in theory) the Sabbat's Elders, and it would make sense that more Sabbat members would head over there than Camarilla members. Many would get dragged along because of their vinculum ties, or simply because killing Elder vampires in the Gehenna Crusade is kind of a big thing that the Sabbat does. It's not hard to imagine that a lot of them would say, &quot;Gehenna is here! Our time has come!&quot; and head off to fight. Personally I intensely dislike the idea of the Beckoning, but this is stuff that makes sense given the context of V5.<br /> <br /> But then the books never did anything else with the Beckoning, due to the fact that it's such a massive world-shaking piece of metaplot that any sort of examination of it is going to take the focus off of the street-level stories that V5 wants players to prioritize. And then apparently Justin is suggesting that the Sabbat elders weren't really affected by the Beckoning and didn't join in the Gehenna War. They're actually still around, and still in charge of the Sabbat, it's just that they decided to implode their own sect and destroy everything they've spent centuries building for reasons - even though the Beckoning and Gehenna War are a pretty solid explanation as to why Sabbat Elders wouldn't be around why the sect would collapse without them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's what Justin wrote about it for points:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://x.com/jachilli/status/1442882322890698752\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://x.com/jachilli/status/1442882322890698752\" target=\"_blank\"> Post Not Found - X | 404 Error </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://x.com/jachilli/status/1442882322890698752\" target=\"_blank\"> https://x.com/jachilli/status/1442882322890698752 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The post you're looking for could not be found or may have been deleted. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">As of V5, the Sabbat is &quot;hollowed out.&quot; It has some elders, it has uncountable neonates and fledglings, but its ancillae are almost entirely absent, casualties of the Gehenna War. The Sabbat strategy is to throw bodies at the problem.<br /> <br /> That's what's behind the disappearance of factions within the Sabbat (Status Quo, Loyalists, Ultra-Conservatives, etc.). The elders don't care about that stuff and the neonates and fledglings never really get a chance to care.</span></i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The &quot;Sword of Cain&quot; sobriquet isn't just coincidence or grandstanding. The elders of the sect use the &quot;Sword&quot; as a tool, a weapon, hurling sect vampires into conflict. It's also a defensive weapon, interposed between the elders wielding it and its enemies.</span></i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">That is, those &quot;guiding&quot; the Sabbat (as it were) know EXACTLY what they're doing with it. (Although, for Storytellers, there doesn't necessarily need to be an elder mastermind in every chronicle. Some and perhaps most domains just end up in the path of destruction.)\u200b</span></i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The big change between editions is that Sabbat sect structure no longer exists in mockery of the Camarilla, as it did in certain legacy editions (VRev/ V20). That's why the book opens with Vykos admonishing the assembled leaders &quot;the way we did things doesn't hold up anymore.</span></i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Straight up, the Sabbat has been WRECKED, crushed between Second Inquisition and Gehenna War. It's eviscerated sect ranks, putting them on the succeed-or-die-trying trajectory. They exist to provoke, and to show the costs of taking the blood-and-fire approach to problem solving.</span></i><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Sabbat book in particular takes this &quot;what's happening NOW?&quot; approach to using them. You can use the legacy-edition materials to help give context, but if you're running a V5 chronicle, you don't need to use that info, and you can plug-and-play introduce them to a chronicle.\u200b</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T01:16:55-07:00","id":1537470,"title":"","content":"In this context, I wonder how the upcoming Gehenna War supplement will fit into this. Because here is what the blurb for the book says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Eternal Struggle at Your Doorstep<br /> <br /> From incessant intrigue to blazing action! Gehenna War brings the machinations of the elders and secret societies to your chronicle. Hunt the elders who were supposedly Beckoned away. Do you fight for the will of an ancient, a chance at the forbidden sin of Diablerie, or to protect what truly matters to you?<br /> <br /> Gehenna War provides material both for players and Storytellers to make the game sing, focusing on fast-paced action and how to weave it into stories and chronicles.<br /> <br /> Gehenna War is a sourcebook for Vampire: The Masquerade, a Storytelling Game of Personal and Political Horror<br /> <br /> Features<ul><li>An overview of the Gehenna War and its impact on the major Kindred sects</li> <li>Rules for creating action-focused characters for action chronicles along with pre-written stories to drop into any chronicle</li> <li>New combat options and equipment and distinct factions fighting in the Gehenna War</li> <li>Advice for using Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals in any chronicle</li> <li>Emphasizes action conflict including chases, gunfights, dueling, infiltration</li> <li>Provides information on new factions</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that this will retcon the Sabbat to still being consumed by the Gehenna War but now it's even more lore-agnostic than before. &quot;Gehenna War&quot; will just mean that in any place at any time packs of Sabbat-vampires might appear to cause chaos and destruction. But as to any bigger take on the Sabbat itself, it will mostly be &quot;Who knows...&quot; and instead it's all just factions and setting-elements you can bring into your game without any wider setting-implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T21:09:15-07:00","id":1537673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537132#post1537132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats a thought terminating cliche and about as a valid as saying all carmarilla games are pretentious theatre kids and larpers or anarchs are just counter culture power fantasies.<br /> <br /> The fact you frame it using d&amp;d terminology which even d&amp;d now downplays highlights how absurd this outlook is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm speaking from experience. Most of the players that wanted to play Sabbat were like that. <br /> <br /> And the theatre-kids who were larpers didn't have power-fantasies. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":10},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T23:39:08-07:00","id":1537679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537673#post1537673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm speaking from experience. Most of the players that wanted to play Sabbat were like that.<br /> <br /> And the theatre-kids who were larpers didn't have power-fantasies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>LARP understands the Baptism by Fire element that I brought up in my Gary Chronicles review, &quot;Being a vampire is inherently cool enough that you can sustain multiple sessions of the PCs just doing vampire things.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T06:36:03-07:00","id":1537700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs#post1536991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, a major allure of V:TM in the first place was playing &quot;the Bad GuyTM.&quot; It was an appeal in the 90s when it first started that you wouldn't be a Lawful Good wandering murderer ala D&amp;D or Call of Cthulhu investigator bound to get eaten. No, you would be a monster struggling wiht their humanity and while some of you would be Angel or Hannibal King, a lot of you would still fall prey to the Beast. So the whole argument the Sabbat should be off-limits doesn't really hold water. It's the same reason playing a Giovanni or Setite is viable even though both of them are every bit as vile as the Sword of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> If WoD was to stay relevant in the current market of RPGs, the creators should remember this and push a bit more this aspect.<br /> It's what would set them apart.<br /> <br /> But if you don't trust your players and think they'll never play it in any more nuanced or interesting way than Grand Theft Auto with Fangs, then it's their loss.<br /> And look I've been in such games, they were badwrongfun. But we were also timid teenagers and probably it was catarthic to play such bad guys, much like violent videogames don't make someone automatically violent<br /> <br /> And absolutely for sure there would be players that would play Grand Theft Auto with Fangs. So?<br /> It's not the totality of their fandom and I don't understand why they care that much.<br /> <br /> Recently I'm reading a lot WtO.<br /> One of the reasons it never took hold I feel it's the risk of succumbing to Shadow and becoming a Spectre was presented (and probably was I never actual played it still sadly) as a much much more real outcome.<br /> <br /> While the risk of wassail and becoming a wight was in VtM but in a more 'yeah it's there' way, but I never saw nor even heard about happening to a real table. Even in the in-character narratives I can't even remember a time when it happened.<br /> <br /> So WtO discouraged you too much from being the monster and do bad things.<br /> Meanwhile Werewolf encouraged you to maul and behead the board of directors of greedy companies, Mage to overthrow the establishment for the greater good (or to defend the establishment for the greater good) with any means, and Sabbat vampires was like to play Near Dark the game as you pointed out.<br /> But I don't want to change topic too much.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is you play the monster, and you do bad things. How much you do it should be single table choice and the game should give the whole range of choice on how much and how often your table will go down that path (including the vampions option).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T08:20:49-07:00","id":1537706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537673#post1537673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm speaking from experience. Most of the players that wanted to play Sabbat were like that.<br /> <br /> And the theatre-kids who were larpers didn't have power-fantasies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty mucy everyone has toxic horror stories, i dont want the brujah gone becauase ive only seen 1 run well in 20 years. Neither am i advocating for the banning of elves in d&amp;d<br /> <br /> Theatre kids have their own issues, ones theyve had 30 years with zero pushback on. They might not be 'power' but theyre perfectly confortable inflicting plot disruption and turgid melodrama on others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-20-2024, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T10:11:35-07:00","id":1537712,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to read other perspectives here, because regarding player archetypes (or stereotypes?) I had them all in every chronicle, regardless whether Sabbat, Cam, or Anarch, P&amp;P or LARP.<br /> Camarilla was pretty much the default setting most of the time and players were mostly looking for political intrigue with a side of action and horror. For Sabbat and Anarchs, games usually had more emphasis on action and for the former, the horror was more splatter than psychological.<br /> <br /> That said, I experienced Sabbat games mostly coming in from the Dark Ages setting, which means the player characters had a very different view on the sects than a current neonate would have. For many the schism was just a convenient tool to cover and push their own interests, and to keep the younglings in line. They really didn't give much of a fig about the divide in philosophies, and the excessive violence was seen as 'wasteful' at best. Personal grudges and feuds outweighed sect allegiance by a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T13:30:21-07:00","id":1537726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537470#post1537470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this context, I wonder how the upcoming Gehenna War supplement will fit into this. Because here is what the blurb for the book says:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My guess is that this will retcon the Sabbat to still being consumed by the Gehenna War but now it's even more lore-agnostic than before. &quot;Gehenna War&quot; will just mean that in any place at any time packs of Sabbat-vampires might appear to cause chaos and destruction. But as to any bigger take on the Sabbat itself, it will mostly be &quot;Who knows...&quot; and instead it's all just factions and setting-elements you can bring into your game without any wider setting-implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...they're just repurposing the &quot;Gehenna Wars&quot; term from the description of the specific series of conflicts in the Middle East that wiped out the Sabbat and most Elders into...a replacement term for traditional Sabbat Crusades.<br /> <br /> Cool, cool. This edition is going great, guys.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunt the elders who were supposedly Beckoned away. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Forget we said anything about all the Elders getting Beckoned away and mulched. Ignore that. They're really super relevant, we swear...please buy our books again.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, no, Paradox. You can't just set fire to the entire setting, and expect us to come crawling back now. You wasted several years of our lives, and killed our beloved characters/factions, only to...steer the entire Vampire metaplot to right where it was before, except objectively crummier and less interesting.<br /> <br /> You could have made the &quot;Gehenna Wars&quot; a playable story <i>in the first place</i>. It's too late now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\u2615","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T18:04:54-07:00","id":1537738,"title":"","content":"Good thing that we can ignore the metaplot and do our own things with it and we still have most of the elders gone away only very few returning but changed in terms power with some being stronger and others seemingly much weaker as if there generation got altered. Not to mention that with the exception of a few die hard war packs the Sabbat has for intents and purpose has collapsed and either joined the Camarilla, Anarchs or become reclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T18:29:32-07:00","id":1537740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537738#post1537738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing that we can ignore the metaplot and do our own things with it and we still have most of the elders gone away only very few returning but changed in terms power with some being stronger and others seemingly much weaker as if there generation got altered. Not to mention that with the exception of a few die hard war packs the Sabbat has for intents and purpose has collapsed and either joined the Camarilla, Anarchs or become reclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing, I don't even think the Beckoning was ever going to get rid of all Elders or someone clearly wasn't paying attention to begin with.<br /> <br /> The back of the main book is full of Elder Loresheets.<br /> <br /> And THE CAMARILLA has a major focus on Victoria Ash and Tegyrius' wedding, which notably are an Elder and muthersucking general of Alexander the Great.<br /> <br /> So did they change their minds about the beckoning or did they never really intend for it to be as big a deal as it was?<br /> <br /> OR was it just something the writers felt they could ignore at will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T10:56:33-07:00","id":1537756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537726#post1537726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So...they're just repurposing the &quot;Gehenna Wars&quot; term from the description of the specific series of conflicts in the Middle East that wiped out the Sabbat and most Elders into...a replacement term for traditional Sabbat Crusades.<br /> <br /> Cool, cool. This edition is going great, guys.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> &quot;Forget we said anything about all the Elders getting Beckoned away and mulched. Ignore that. They're really super relevant, we swear...please buy our books again.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, no, Paradox. You can't just set fire to the entire setting, and expect us to come crawling back now. You wasted several years of our lives, and killed our beloved characters/factions, only to...steer the entire Vampire metaplot to right where it was before, except objectively crummier and less interesting.<br /> <br /> You could have made the &quot;Gehenna Wars&quot; a playable story <i>in the first place</i>. It's too late now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what's important for context here is that Juhana Pettersson is now the lead-developer and his background is all about Nordic LARP. And so... we're gonna get a WOD5E heavily influenced by Nordic LARP for the foreseeable future (like the section about Bleed-hunting in Blood-Stained Love, for example). And that of course comes into conflict with the way things have been presented before in corebooks or supplements. But it doesn't seem like anybody working on these books over at Paradox and Renegade cares enough to worry about that. We already got Sabbat-lite with the Church of Caine in Crimson Gutter as well under that new leadership. By comparison, Justin Achilli's take had been that V5 should be about playing young Anarchs - and <i>only </i>that. It was part of his whole paradigm for WOD5E as shown by H5 letting you <i>only </i>play street-level hunter-cells.<br /> <br /> But yeah, for the edition as a whole... what a mess...<br /> <br /> For example, Renegade recently announced they're gonna sell a reprint of &quot;Revelations Of The Dark Mother&quot; for a whopping 40 bucks. It wouldn't surprise me if they're going to do a reprint of &quot;The Silver Record&quot;-book for WtA as well in the future (despite the whole &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-thingy).<br /> <br /> Personally, I think I like Juhana Pettersson's tenure more so far than when Justin Achilli was the lead-developer but looking at these books as supposedly being part of the same edition... Man, that's just depressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T11:01:33-07:00","id":1537757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537756#post1537756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what's important for context here is that Juhana Pettersson is now the lead-developer and his background is all about Nordic LARP. And so... we're gonna get a WOD5E heavily influenced by Nordic LARP for the foreseeable future (like the section about Bleed-hunting in Blood-Stained Love, for example). And that of course comes into conflict with the way things have been presented before in corebooks or supplements. But it doesn't seem like anybody working on these books over at Paradox and Renegade cares enough to worry about that. We already got Sabbat-lite with the Church of Caine in Crimson Gutter as well under that new leadership. By comparison, Justin Achilli's take had been that V5 should be about playing young Anarchs - and <i>only </i>that. It was part of his whole paradigm for WOD5E as shown by H5 letting you <i>only </i>play street-level hunter-cells.<br /> <br /> But yeah, for the edition as a whole... what a mess...<br /> <br /> For example, Renegade recently announced they're gonna sell a reprint of &quot;Revelations Of The Dark Mother&quot; for a whopping 40 bucks. It wouldn't surprise me if they're going to do a reprint of &quot;The Silver Record&quot;-book for WtA as well in the future (despite the whole &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-thingy).<br /> <br /> Personally, I think I like Juhana Pettersson's tenure more so far than when Justin Achilli was the lead-developer but looking at these books as supposedly being part of the same edition... Man, that's just depressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Revelations of the Dark Mother thing is extra funny because I think you can still buy a reprint for ten bucks.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli got fired/unhired after the Sabbat book as well, so its probably not fair to blame him much either. I get the impression that he, too, had a bunch of ideas that were ordered on the cutting room floor ala Zach Snyder.<br /> <br /> He was never a big Anarch fan either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T11:22:32-07:00","id":1537758,"title":"","content":"It's probably that someone wasn't paying attention what was written before and that is not a new thing in this industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T11:26:48-07:00","id":1537760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537757#post1537757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Revelations of the Dark Mother thing is extra funny because I think you can still buy a reprint for ten bucks.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli got fired/unhired after the Sabbat book as well, so its probably not fair to blame him much either. I get the impression that he, too, had a bunch of ideas that were ordered on the cutting room floor ala Zach Snyder.<br /> <br /> He was never a big Anarch fan either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he was the lead-developer, so it's his name on it. At the end of the day, unless he comes forward he's gonna be the poster-child for the whole thing - justly or unjustly as it may be. With the Fenrir-thing in W5 it's clear he was fudging the truth a little bit in what was going on behind the scenes. Of course, that doesn't mean he's solely to blame. But without him coming forward and telling us what went on, we only have the books and the books list him as lead-developer. And the tweets he put out. But the way he left during the development of the W5 corebook was also a bit unusual.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I always had the same feeling that if it had been completely up to him things would've been different. At this point, though, I don't think it's right to blame any one person individually. Throughout the whole course of WOD5E, throughout all the mishaps and scandals, the one constant has been Paradox. The way they've been managing the franchise and the people working on it has led to way more problems than there should've been. And I think the issue is bigger than who the current lead-developer for the WOD5E-books is. But yeah, now we got Juhana Pettersson and hey, another difference: He's working for Renegade and isn't part of the Paradox-in-house team (who even knows why this changed...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T11:32:10-07:00","id":1537762,"title":"","content":"Just like putting the sole blame on the fall of WCW on Eric Bischoff, Hulk Hogan and Kevin Nash and not acknowledge that the problems went way beyond them and the company wasn't well run and was losing more money then it was making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T20:16:04-07:00","id":1537780,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:9px\">TLDR: Vykos in V5 is fake. Real Vykos woulnd't be caught dead with that rabble. Where is Vykos? Not there. Are they well? Yes. It is still fucking weird that Lucita is in the True Sabbat, after so many centuries hating each other. Yes.<br /> He was weirded out before too.</span> <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:9px\"><i>That's what's behind the disappearance of factions within the Sabbat (Status Quo, Loyalists, Ultra-Conservatives, etc.). The elders don't care about that stuff and the neonates and fledglings never really get a chance to care.</i></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Elders cared about this. Because there were three hundred thousand fucking shovelheads and getting more.<br /> The Loyalists didn't. &quot;Girls just wanna have fun&quot;, but the. loyalists aren't even the fun, let's experiment on a few dozen people and make ourselves more biologically study and adapted to space...<br /> No... they just wanna, to smash, drink, etc, basically Russian mercenary soldiers that came straight from the death row to wage war in Ukraine.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">The same ones who ripped the Code of Milan apart... like they dreamed of<br /> <br /> Only salvation for this man, if he meant the TMR elders. Because plenty of them are older than the Sabbat's 1000-year old club. And they certainly didn't care.<br /> <br /> But I'm glad he confirmed, that the False Sabbat have a few elders (TMR imported stuff) and a bunch of young idiots.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The &quot;Sword of Cain&quot; sobriquet isn't just coincidence or grandstanding. The elders of the sect use the &quot;Sword&quot; as a tool, a weapon, hurling sect vampires into conflict. It's also a defensive weapon, interposed between the elders wielding it and its enemies.</i> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">This is also a TMR reference. HMMMM... After all, we've had out into the Sabbat heads, from the books. But guess who used the Sword as a weapon against cam and anarchs and vice versa, vice versa.<br /> <br /> They have SO many TMR references in the story.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>That is, those &quot;guiding&quot; the Sabbat (as it were) know EXACTLY what they're doing with it. </i> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Hm.....Again... sounds a lot like Sabbat as of BJD</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The big change between editions is that Sabbat sect structure no longer exists in mockery of the Camarilla, as it did in certain legacy editions (VRev/ V20). That's why the book opens with Vykos admonishing the assembled leaders &quot;the way we did things doesn't hold up anymore.</i> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">I don't know if anyone told him, but there are only a limited amount of societal structures that function well.<br /> And not like they changed anything in it anyway.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> But, if the Old Sabbat found out about TMR, would it be trolling/scaring Camarilla cities? Nah nah nah,<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>---radio static ---&quot;Target acquired, good hunting Sabbat brethren. Happy fucking Purge Day. Here... kitty kitty...&quot; --- malkavian laughter ---</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> As for...structures of how Cainite society, and Sabbat too. Literally, the first law of development, &quot;if it ain't broke don't fix it&quot;. Second law, &quot;Don't invent a fucking bike.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Sabbat had at least a proto-constitution.<br /> <br /> As for holding city domains... Caine invented a city. So who are we to question Daddy Caine.<br /> <br /> Second, there are literally so few social ways for vampires to organize, without shit falling apart. Guess what... if it ain't broke, don't fucking fix it. <hr />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28432,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28432-misskaos22","user":"MissKaos22","date":". 08-06-2024, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28432-misskaos22","name":"MissKaos22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28432_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T12:27:56-07:00","id":1537869,"title":"","content":"I hope future sourcebooks will improve in quality and we can people like Gentleman Gamer helping out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T19:03:17-07:00","id":1538162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537869#post1537869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope future sourcebooks will improve in quality and we can people like Gentleman Gamer helping out.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what little I know behind the scenes, I think Paradox has burned a lot of bridges with many talented established authors who know the setting.<br /> <br /> But who knows, they're all professionals after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":6},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T19:27:18-07:00","id":1538163,"title":"","content":"How unprofessional some people can be in the entertainment industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T00:41:09-07:00","id":1539739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1538163#post1538163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How unprofessional some people can be in the entertainment industry.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have no idea. I can't disclose which, but a french RPG editor is basically hamstrung on its golden goose product because they have toxic management and no contracts with the main author who is thus keeping the next two books worth of writing she did and/or supervised.<br /> <br /> Entertainment industry often rely on enthusiastic workers coming in, accepting shitty practices because of passion and then ditching them to replace them with younger ones when they get burnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T16:28:29-07:00","id":1539808,"title":"","content":"So basically every job under the sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T19:01:44-07:00","id":1539908,"title":"","content":"To the original topic and also shameless plug...this might be of help to make well crafted sabbat PCs instead of murder hobos!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/490675/Daughters-and-Sons-of-Caine?src=newest_community&amp;filters=45622_45629\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...rs=45622_45629</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T13:03:30-07:00","id":1540217,"title":"","content":"I should see if I can find that book somewhere and get more ideas for the few remaining packs that we have in our game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T18:19:17-07:00","id":1540540,"title":"","content":"Without reading this entire thread, I disagree with its entire premise. The issue wasn't with the Sabbat. It was with its players, myself included. I remember way back when in 1852 when they first came out, my and my game group gleefully got together every Friday night with a case of beer, and a head full of 20 yr old visions of horror. These days, the kids would call it &quot;cringe&quot;. We all sat there and &quot;roleplayed&quot; our cringiest gross-out fantasies and drunkenly tried to make our friends cry. And as stupid as it was, it was <b><i>fun. </i></b>These days, we've become more sophisticated, nuanced, mature. The times have changed as well. Could you imagine the hubbub when a stream shows players giggling while they imagine kick-fucking babies down main street with my edgy Tzimisc-ombra with my trenchcoat with a cock fleshcrafted to my forehead cause I want my enemies to see exactly how hard all this dumb shit got me. As we grew older we wanted to relive the fun...not necessarily the cringe, but the fun.<br /> <br /> So the older more &quot;mature&quot; me looks at the Sabbat and sees true horror. religious extremists. Those who will stop at nothing to get your attention and make you see &quot;God&quot; <i>My way is the only way all other ideas are heresy, and no matter what you say or do join or die.</i> <i>&quot;Caine akbar! &quot;&quot;Caine vult!&quot;</i> - pick your poison for your game, the devil came be whatever you want it to be, but whatever it is, it is &quot;god&quot; and i<i>ts worth killing everyone for; and worth dying for. Humans are cattle and Camarilla are pretty much the same- &quot;Heathens&quot;, the blind.</i><br /> <br /> With this line of thinking, it makes the Anarchs necessary. Anarchs are bad...malcontents, rebels, but they at least <b>kinda share our</b> morality. Not like the monsters, the religious zealots that are the sabbat. This also means the sabbat are not mindless monsters. They are worse. They are calculating monsters. They are &quot;the enemy&quot; they hate our values, our very state of being and will stop at nothing to destroy us and our ways.<br /> <br /> Look at the real world. The middle east hates the western world, our core values, way of life etc. The extremists, though at a disadvantage continue to resist. Violence comes easy. Why? easy. Their values are different than ours. We see conflict and shake our fists seeing dead children, screaming about injustice. But, <i>thats through our eyes and our morals. We weren't raised with their line of thinking. </i>One could argue that the West is wrong, trying to push our values on others, or vice versa. Here's our paths of enlightenment. Different clans, &quot;tribes&quot; seeing things differently but in line with one central thought. <i>Caine is right. The Antediluvians WILL kill us all.</i> This isn't up for debate. This is scripture. And if you deny or question it, you are helping. Its you or me bud and I won't have your toxic ideals influencing my childer. I'll kill you first. I'll kill everyone first <i>(I know this comes off as very anti muslim, but thats not the intent. In fact, the Christians did the exact same thing over the Crusades I'd argue its human nature and the nature of the radical faithful)</i><br /> <br /> My older, more mature self see's this and gets excited to play. Wants to have the heated debates with my friends within the confines of the game. To challenge and be challenged. To try to wrap my mind around ideals that are foreign to me. To be the &quot;monster&quot; more than your standard blood drinking licks. But I can also understand a business like Paradox, looking at this and saying, &quot;after all the heat we've gotten there is no way in hell can we condone this. BUT there is huge demand for it so lets put it out there as the 'enemy'. People will be smart enough to figure it out...besides...think of the cost of the page count!&quot; In the era of streaming, companies have to be super careful and sacrifice elements to avoid heat. And god knows vtm has brought enough to Paradox...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently running: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279855-chicago-gary-by-night-omerta-players-probably-want-to-skip-this-post\" target=\"_blank\">Gary/Chicago By Night</a>","edited":{"userid":1263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1263-schwartzung","user":"Schwartzung","date":".  added last paragraph 08-16-2024, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1263-schwartzung","name":"Schwartzung","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T11:45:54-07:00","id":1540994,"title":"","content":"Sabbat can be, like anything else, whatever you want them to be. Sects tend to be more of a perspective IMO.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sabbat can be played as the typical murderhobo. It's fun.<br /> <br /> Sabbat can be played as victim of very shitty circumstance.<br /> <br /> Play as a random shovelhead. Seriously. It's very under rated.<br /> <br /> Pick a totally normies vanilla character:<br /> <br /> Some highschool gym teacher. He got clanged on the head and digs himself out to find out he's now a suicide shock troop in a fanatical cult that is using him as a meat shield. If he survived the assault he gets to be a made man in this nonsensical cult of monsters. <br /> <br /> Or play Grandma Flo, who got clanged as she went out for cat food. <br /> <br /> Maybe these characters hate what has happened and look for ANY way out should the valuderie get a bit weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T12:10:47-07:00","id":1540996,"title":"","content":"Interestedly enough I think they had a Lasombra archtype that was a grandmother who survived the mass embrace in there revised clanbook or was it in the Sabbat sourcebook? Either way she had an interesting description on how to depict her in a game and how she dealt with pack relationships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T16:24:18-07:00","id":1541038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1540996#post1540996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestedly enough I think they had a Lasombra archtype that was a grandmother who survived the mass embrace in there revised clanbook or was it in the Sabbat sourcebook? Either way she had an interesting description on how to depict her in a game and how she dealt with pack relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah she was one of the lasombra suggestions.<br /> <br /> Big advantage if mass embraces is it really opens who is in what clan. Last sabbat lasombra was a cheerleader gone bad who actually did quite well for herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T18:31:20-07:00","id":1541045,"title":"","content":"A Lasombra cheerleader is a fun visual and open to so many storytelling options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T10:17:22-07:00","id":1541070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541045#post1541045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lasombra cheerleader is a fun visual and open to so many storytelling options.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Amici Noctis</b> think <i>they </i>are viscous, backstabbing, cadre dedicated to suborning those they view as their lessers and wielding power with ruthless efficiency for self promotion.<br /> <br /> The popular girls clique at any given high-school would give them daymares for weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T12:38:41-07:00","id":1541076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541038#post1541038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big advantage if mass embraces is it really opens who is in what clan. Last sabbat lasombra was a cheerleader gone bad who actually did quite well for herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thinking about the Sabbat is firmly based on the impact of mass embraces and the example pack found in second edition Chicago By Night.<br /> <br /> For Camarilla and Anarch vampires, the emphasis is usually on what was it about their mortal life that interested their sire to embrace them. The reasons might be trivial or profound, but usually there is a reason. When designing their character, most players will think hard about that and why and how their PC will fit into their clan based on their mortal history. There is a continuity between their mortal life and their existence as a vampire.<br /> <br /> For Sabbat vampires though, the emphasis is how they reacted after their turning. Instead of continuity, there is an abrupt departure.<br /> <br /> This is what we see in Cameron's Nomad pack.<br /> <br /> Cameron himself was a scrawny hypochondriac loser. His Panhandling Talent implies he was likely living on the streets when he was embraced. Yet somehow he survived the creation rites, became the only surviving member of his pack, and eventually rose to be ductus. Of course, to his clanmates in the Lasombra, Cameron remains an embarrassment and they can't understand why this guy survived. So they send him off on a mission that is mean to fail and probably get him killed. Yet by looking at his stats and history, there isn't much evidence that he's been a failure as a vampire. It's just that to other Lasombra he doesn't fit the mold. Yeah, he's relying on Tyler to tell him what to do, but it's his first experience with being any kind of leader. He has to grow into it, and it wasn't like he was groomed or prepared for these responsibilities. Even if he fails at being a leader, it's not like that is the sole criteria by which to judge a Lasombra. He has minimal Leadership Talent, but has a very high Manipulation. That implies he would do well in other scenarios.<br /> <br /> Lolita was an orphan who spent her whole life in the foster care system being passed around from one family to the next. Now she's aiming to move up in clan and sect Status, having confidence and opportunities as a vampire she never had in life.<br /> <br /> Margarite was fresh out of high school looking forward to finding a future husband so she could have kids in a house with a white picket fence. Now she cares absolutely nothing about those dreams and is completely dedicated to being a vampire and member of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Of course, we already had some of that with Wendy Wade who went from being a young, successful lawyer who was embraced only because she was at the wrong place at the wrong time. But with Wendy, we can see why she was being successful as a vampire based on her mortal history. With Cameron's pack, we're seeing some surprises. Now the nomad pack as a whole is supposed to be a bunch of misfits, but I don't see why any of them could not have been considered a successful Sabbat member if they were integrated in a more successful pack. Nor do I think putting together &quot;misfits&quot; into a new pack and sending them off is anything unique. This is probably standard modus operandi for the sect.<br /> <br /> To me, this is the big thing distinguishing the Sabbat from all the others. The others are still concerned about getting the &quot;right&quot; childe and use their mortal life as an indicator for their fitness. The Sabbat instead has the attitude that their mortal life is unimportant and doesn't reflect how well they might adjust. Just embrace anyone and see what happens - people will surprise you. It is a good way to distinguish the sects.<br /> <br /> The examples of the nomad pack cemented certain ideas of what Sabbat vampires were like, and that did fit how the sect was described in the Players and Storytellers Guides. It's a big reason why I dislike the Lasombra and Tzimisce clanbooks. They were written from the perspective that those clans were actually more like the Camarilla in clans in how they embrace new vampires. I don't recall any of their PC templates/examples reflecting that a substantial number of them would be random embraces. I didn't mind to see that some embraces would be &quot;traditional&quot;, but completely ignoring the creation rites created a very bad impression in players. And that is why we saw the erosion of distinctive Sabbat elements in Revised (other than a general splatterpunk). The mass embrace should be the typical while the traditional embrace should be the exception within the Sabbat IMO. (The many examples of traditional embraces in the clanbooks would often make good Lasmobra anti-tribu or Old Clan Tzimisce (if not for the Viccisitude), but are out of place for the Sabbat.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T13:45:03-07:00","id":1541079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcusVitel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541070#post1541070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Amici Noctis</b> think <i>they </i>are viscous, backstabbing, cadre dedicated to suborning those they view as their lessers and wielding power with ruthless efficiency for self promotion.<br /> <br /> The popular girls clique at any given high-school would give them daymares for weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that was the logic, you have the a driven, focused, social individual in good physical health at time of embrace.<br /> Another interesting example of this was a middle class crufts competator who became a fiend and did very well in terms of various hellhounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T12:10:03-07:00","id":1541210,"title":"","content":"Artists would make good Fiends in general when you think about it Ragged Robin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T06:21:56-07:00","id":1541226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541210#post1541210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artists would make good Fiends in general when you think about it Ragged Robin.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fiends are actually very flexible in terms of whose clan material. They only need to be hyper focused, intelligent and comfortable devaluing others.<br /> <br /> Something a GM I know who runs a lot of Sabbat does is they create a distinction between people who just happen to a member of the clan vs those who 'fit in'. This creates an interesting dynamic were clan culture becomes more a choice rather than something enforced. For example my Cheerleader gone bad fitted very comfortably in the Keepers wereas the tzmisce hank hill style engineer just happened to a fiend but other clan mates didn't really call him out on not being a depraved sadistic maniac.<br /> <br /> &quot;well he shares our blood and did a great job fitting my security cameras. We ultimately consider such members more like distant family members who don't get invited to thanksgiving because they wouldn't want to come anyway. No harm no foul, let us know if you think your childer would fit in&quot;-Tzmisce Boyar in game about 'hank'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T14:40:49-07:00","id":1541246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541226#post1541226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something a GM I know who runs a lot of Sabbat does is they create a distinction between people who just happen to a member of the clan vs those who 'fit in'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is very appropriate for the Sabbat. The Sabbat lack the NCO core of ancillae as very few Sabbat neonates live that long. So clan culture is something that elders perpetuate among themselves. Whether Sabbat neonates &quot;fit in&quot; or are &quot;misfits&quot; is almost immaterial. Very few will live long enough. Only those few who become ancilla would be worth time and effort to cultivate. And likely only those surviving neonates who fit into the culture would get any kind of support or mentoring that might help them survive until then. The worst misfits might even be assigned dangerous tasks (&quot;It's a great opportunity!&quot;) that would likely get them killed.<br /> <br /> Those misfits who do survive and gain power in the sect likely gravitate as minority clan members who either become Loyalists, or perhaps join one of the other factions where clan loyalties are not a block to advancement like the Sabbat Inquisition, Black Hand, become a secret infernalist, or become a templar/paladin.<br /> <br /> An emphasis on clan culture is really something that the hypocritical elders are concerned about, it's not really important to the Sabbat as a sect. It actually represents something the sect - supposedly - rebelled against in the Anarch Revolt. Clan divisions are just another way the elders divide and conquer the neonates. At least that is the unstated, but generic attitude of the sect that I try to present as ST. That the elder leaders of the sect still perpetuate its importance is unacknowledged, but present. So clan culture is acknowledged but downplayed in public, while being important behind closed doors but not stated outright.<br /> <br /> My main concern as an ST in regards to the Sabbat is to present a very different sect culture and feeling than among the Camarilla or anarchs. So emphasizing pack culture, the paths of enlightenment, and the unique institutions of the Sabbat is more important to me than the clans of characters. I've seen too many Sabbat games where characters are not distinguishable from the Camarilla except that they are much more bloodthirsty and use different titles. I think that does a disservice to the ideas behind the sect. I want the portrayal of the Sabbat to be truly alien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  mentioned the paths 08-30-2024, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T15:49:44-07:00","id":1541249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541246#post1541246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is very appropriate for the Sabbat. The Sabbat lack the NCO core of ancillae as very few Sabbat neonates live that long. So clan culture is something that elders perpetuate among themselves. Whether Sabbat neonates &quot;fit in&quot; or are &quot;misfits&quot; is almost immaterial. Very few will live long enough. Only those few who become ancilla would be worth time and effort to cultivate. And likely only those surviving neonates who fit into the culture would get any kind of support or mentoring that might help them survive until then. The worst misfits might even be assigned dangerous tasks (&quot;It's a great opportunity!&quot;) that would likely get them killed.<br /> <br /> Those misfits who do survive and gain power in the sect likely gravitate as minority clan members who either become Loyalists, or perhaps join one of the other factions where clan loyalties are not a block to advancement like the Sabbat Inquisition, Black Hand, become a secret infernalist, or become a templar/paladin.<br /> <br /> An emphasis on clan culture is really something that the hypocritical elders are concerned about, it's not really important to the Sabbat as a sect. It actually represents something the sect - supposedly - rebelled against in the Anarch Revolt. Clan divisions are just another way the elders divide and conquer the neonates. At least that is the unstated, but generic attitude of the sect that I try to present as ST. That the elder leaders of the sect still perpetuate its importance is unacknowledged, but present. So clan culture is acknowledged but downplayed in public, while being important behind closed doors but not stated outright.<br /> <br /> My main concern as an ST in regards to the Sabbat is to present a very different sect culture and feeling than among the Camarilla or anarchs. So emphasizing pack culture, the paths of enlightenment, and the unique institutions of the Sabbat is more important to me than the clans of characters. I've seen too many Sabbat games where characters are not distinguishable from the Camarilla except that they are much more bloodthirsty and use different titles. I think that does a disservice to the ideas behind the sect. I want the portrayal of the Sabbat to be truly alien.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, the gm would probably frown at the idea of 'good' sabbat culture vs 'bad' clan culture-something which would be a bit reductive as a 'correct' play option<br /> More that you as a player of how you persue your sabbat experiance im were you lean into. I recall a serpant pc who was ultimatly indifferant from both in contrast to another who climbed in line, path and sect.<br /> <br /> Im also a little surprised to hear the clans as an obstruction to the alienness of the sabbat considering clans are completly distinct from human experiance and a large number of the clans and bloodlines act as a medium to articulate that inhumanity. Notably the big 2.<br /> <br /> To say nothing off pretty much all the sabbat clan write ups being awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-30-2024, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T00:36:43-07:00","id":1541270,"title":"","content":"I just think that it's better that pack culture and the Paths of Enlightenment should be more dominant for Sabbat characters than clans. I remember when Montreal By Night came out, and the base organization for characters was by pack instead of by clan. I think that was a good choice, and it remained with me ever since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T00:50:55-07:00","id":1541271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541270#post1541270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think that it's better that pack culture and the Paths of Enlightenment should be more dominant for Sabbat characters than clans. I remember when Montreal By Night came out, and the base organization for characters was by pack instead of by clan. I think that was a good choice, and it remained with me ever since.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont consider it a binary. Im also genrally reluctant to commit to a single aspect as the definitive trait especially as most vtm games revolve around coterie/pack including tower and movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-31-2024, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T08:37:29-07:00","id":1541289,"title":"","content":"Multiple editions' diluting the Sabbat's identity is the issue. I mean, when you say Sabbat, <i>which</i> Sabbat do you mean?<br /> <br /> 1. Losers from the first Anarch revolt who just wanted a vampiric society of their own, but locked themselves and their descendants into cycles of violence and revenge against the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> 2. The mishmash of heretical and eschatonic cults based on major world religions and Noddism?<br /> <br /> 3. Vampire separatists and supremacists who embrace the Beast and their own monstrosity?<br /> <br /> 4. Those (mostly neonates and ancilla) who are just kind of along for the ride, and amount to slightly edgier and more ultraviolent Anarchs?<br /> <br /> 5. Serial diablerists and other degenerates who are for all intents and purposes wights, but retain enough of their &quot;higher&quot; selves to function on a pack level?<br /> <br /> Each aspects' focus changed depending on edition, and it never quite seemed like writers could decide who or what the Sabbat really was at its core. Ultimately, the Sabbat is a dysfunctional society held together only by the threat of their own elders and methuselahs, the threat of the Camarilla, and the vaulderie.<br /> <br /> <i>[Yes, you could say the same of the Camarilla being a dysfunctional society held together by the threat of their own elders and methuselahs, the threat of the Sabbat, and prestation...and the Anarchs are a dysfunctional society held together by the threat of the Camarilla and Sabbat.]</i><br /> <br /> When it comes to my games I like to emphasize points three and four, with points one and two being the Sabbat's connective tissue, and point five being its (unintended) self-regulatory mechanism. To me, at the end of the day the Sabbat became what it intended to fight: a tyrannical elder supremacist sect that maintains control by keeping neonates and ancillae distracted with external threats. Sabbat elders have more in common with Camarilla elders than the younger vampires of their own sect, and are more than happy to throw an entire city to the fire in a manufactured and curated conflict to preserve their own existence and station. All else -- religion, politics, whatever -- is simply kayfabe and delusion.<br /> <br /> To me, that makes Sabbat <i>and</i> Camarilla more interesting: Camarilla vampires on Paths of Enlightenment (or even Roads), hypocritically enforcing Humanity on their lessers as a mechanism for control. Sabbat elders carefully hiding and preserving Humanity, going to elaborate lengths to make themselves appear monstrous while never actually being such. Elders and even ancillae with alliances across sect boundaries, engaging in quid pro quo or even manipulating entire sieges for mutual benefit. The careful dance of a manufactured sect war that really isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T00:36:33-07:00","id":1541323,"title":"","content":"The difficultybif universal definition actually makes sense. the idea of the sect/s as a universal concept isnt really viable. If anything the big issue with 5th ed writting is the idea you have to do this really reductive &quot;summerise the group in a verb or two&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe large complex social groups cant really be defined in a sentance?<br /> <br /> Edit-thinking on it, its actually quite interesting that out of the three sects the carmarilla is genrally the only one people are genrally happy with. The anarchs are underwritten while people are obsessed with what the sword are 'supposed' to be. For example clans or corruption are never challanged in the tower like they are in the others and everyone seems happy with how the tower games go.<br /> the only objection ive seen is the shift to stupid evil rather than pragmatic evil in v5 but this is very superficial and doesnt generate debate like the other two do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-01-2024, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T08:06:43-07:00","id":1541335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541323#post1541323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...its actually quite interesting that out of the three sects the carmarilla is genrally the only one people are genrally happy with. The anarchs are underwritten while people are obsessed with what the sword are 'supposed' to be. For example clans or corruption are never challanged in the tower like they are in the others and everyone seems happy with how the tower games go.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really surprising, though. This actually came up just last night with my partner, as she and I finished AMC's <i>Interview with the Vampire's</i> second season last time we hung out, she recently finished reading The Vampire Chronicles, and I've been explaining VtM to her bit-by-bit. Here's how I got her tracking by sect:<br /> <br /> Sabbat: Akasha's end-of-the-world-as-we-know-it cult, but medieval Catholic-flavored even down to its own vampire pope and inquisition. In practice they act somewhere between Theatre des Vampires, Russell Edgington from True Blood, and Alex's droogs from <i>A Clockwork Orange</i>.<br /> <br /> Anarchs: it's a chaotic mishmash of countercultures and countercultural political movements that are held together only by the common thread of not being mainstream. All claim some form of libertarianism or anarchism, but at the end of the day pecking order is determined by might-makes-right.<br /> <br /> Camarilla: Vampire UN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T16:00:56-07:00","id":1541364,"title":"","content":"I think part of it is that the Cam (&amp; to a lesser extent the Anarchs) have a similar vibe to the OG 7* clans where elements of them may get criticized from time to time but they\u2019re far less likely to get the question of \u2018should we ignore these entirely?\u2019 that both the Sabbat &amp; Independent clans sometimes get <br /> <br /> *admittedly this is less true abt the Malkavians &amp; Tremere, both draw their fair share of controversy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T18:36:56-07:00","id":1541372,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, I believe the purpose of the Sabbat is to allow the World of Darkness to have pre-Anne Rice vampires. The kind we all know from movies and literature where the vampire shows up, turns random people into vampires, and devours the community until the hunters destroy him. The Camarilla was for post-modern vampires where vampires could be protagonists, perhaps even heroes. So the game covered both angles. The Sabbat also played the role of the bogeyman in a setting dominated by the Camarilla, but increasingly under threat. As long as you do that, you've succeeded at a general level. <br /> <br /> The issue is how do you distinguish the Sabbat from the Camarilla so they are truly different? If you just make them like the Camarilla, it opens the question of why those anarchs at the Convention of Thorns just didn't just join up anyway? Why go through the long centuries of initial defeat when they were routed from most of Europe to flee to the Americas only to self-destruct in three civil wars? The terrifying Sabbat we know from the sourcebooks only really began in 1957 when the Third Civil War ended, or at best 1933 when the Second Civil War ended and the revised Code of Milan was established.<br /> <br /> That Sabbat is very different from the original anarchs who defied the Camarilla by leaving the Convention of Thorns. The Sabbat has always been a big mess. That's part of its appeal. It gives the ST a lot of different tools to tailor her chronicles. Emphasizing Paths of Enlightenment, pack cultures as an institution, internal Sabbat politics of radical freedom versus warfighting needs, and so on provides the tools for the ST to distinguish the sect from the Camarilla. An individual Sabbat domain could be vastly different from another one. I think the trouble occurs from a setting design perspective whenever the publisher decides only ONE way to portray the Sabbat was the one true way, and invalidates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T19:14:57-07:00","id":1541374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1540996#post1540996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestedly enough I think they had a Lasombra archtype that was a grandmother who survived the mass embrace in there revised clanbook or was it in the Sabbat sourcebook? Either way she had an interesting description on how to depict her in a game and how she dealt with pack relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the point her write-up made that she was a new-ish vampire, but had many decades of life experience to call on, unlike most pretty young things embraced from the nightclub crowd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T09:52:50-07:00","id":1541397,"title":"","content":"Neonates with way more life experiences can be more dangerous because of that. A good pop culture example is season 3 of Buffy where Angel deals with the Mayor and you can see how the baddie words struck the right spots against Angel.<br /> <br /> Angel was a supernatural being much longer than the Mayor, but he was human much longer before he made his plans for ascension. In more recent years I've been thinking he was one of the better villains of the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T12:43:57-07:00","id":1541476,"title":"","content":"I would never make this the only way to play the Sabbat but for our Transylvania Chronicles, we had a lot of fun with the concept of <b>&quot;The Sabbat as the failure of communism&quot;</b>. Which is a weird premise but was an interesting thing to explore when you start as Anarchs in the Dark Ages and move to the late Nineties where you see the collapse of the Soviet Union and other non-capitalist ideologies.<br /> <br /> The idea of the campaign we played circa 1999-2004 was the idea that the Anarchs who refused to bend the knee at Thorns were actually sincere in their desire for freedom as well as building a better Kindred society. However, they immediately are confronted with the fact the rest of their kind doesn't care about that and are only interested in building their own power bases.<br /> <br /> Eventually, by the year 1999, the Sabbat is falling apart due to the corrupted Paths of Enlightenment and massive blood bonding and fanaticism that makes it worse than the Camarilla ever was. It's going to collapse in a couple of decades no matter what the players do and they can either try to start something new, reform the existing one, or leave a sinking ship behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T15:04:25-07:00","id":1541487,"title":"","content":"In our game I mentioned that the Sabbat crumbled because of the realization of that there actions against the 3rd generation were meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T08:39:53-07:00","id":1541533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541397#post1541397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neonates with way more life experiences can be more dangerous because of that...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say &quot;can be&quot;, but it's a fringe case that absolutely can and should be explored. Hell, in the chronicle I was running about which I've spoken recently before, this specifically came up and I had great pleasure subverting it.<br /> <br /> Long story short, Hecata PC who was an older gent, was growing increasingly exasperated by the juvenile behavior of vampires decades older than him, and the dumb immature shenanigans constantly happening around him. He figured a lot of this would be more easily and peacefully resolved by everyone just sitting everyone down for an adult conversation. Enter one of the Gangrel NPC's, who took him to &quot;play golf&quot; after that night's matches were over. Hecata got even more pissed when he found out golf had nothing to do with it -- the Gangrel just started driving balls into a nearby subdivision as an act of petty vandalism.<br /> <br /> The Hecata's grievance came down to &quot;you have all the time and power in the world, why are you wasting it with a bunch of stupid pointless shit instead of solving problems and doing things that matter?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which, the PC was absolutely right and his grievances are justified. The NPC's were up to a <i>hell</i> of a lot of really dumb, pointless, immature shit. That includes his own (technically a methuselah) sire, who has done nothing except sit on his ass in his haven watching TV, only coming out when absolutely necessary or upon inducement with some other wonder of modern civilization. Then came the lesson (which I'll paraphrase):<br /> <br /> You have <i>life</i> experience, but the people you're complaining about have <i>unlife</i> experience.<br /> <br /> Your perspective doesn't reflect a vampire's existence yet. Humans are mortal, and the older they get the more acutely they feel their mortality. Human drive, ambition, and pride are functions of mortality: it's just a race against time to make your mark on the world before you kick off one way or the other. Neonates still feel that vestigially, but after the first couple decades of not aging, not getting sick, not having to eat or shit, and having a bunch of cool supernatural powers to do with as one pleases, and once all the mortals you knew in life die off...there's just no longer time pressure to accomplish anything. Once you have yours, that's it.<br /> <br /> Boredom sets in, and vampires have to find anything they can to stave it off. Dumb college pranks, bullying each other, curating grudges, petty vandalism, getting unhealthily obsessed with the dumbest aspects of mortal popular culture, turning mortals against each other to sit back and watch: it's all just to have something to do. Solving problems just means you have fewer things with which to occupy yourself; even if it's unconsciously, vampires <i>will</i> self-sabotage just to keep that &quot;shit to do&quot; list full. As such, adult conversations just don't (and will never) work with vampires -- they're antithetical to the search for meaning in vampiric existence.<br /> <br /> To you, it looks like a bunch of stupid pointless shit that misses the point. And objectively, that's true. But to us, it's the only reason we have to wake up at night. Immortality's a bitch.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, the Hecata PC was <i>deeply</i> unhappy with that answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T14:40:09-07:00","id":1541546,"title":"","content":"Messing with each other and collecting boons and or lore is what drives them after a few centuries of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T21:41:24-07:00","id":1541944,"title":"","content":"The best villains, in my opinion, are the ones who are convinced they are righteous and validated, no matter how repulsive their motives may be to humanity in general.<br /> <br /> I hate to cite shitty pop culture fiction characters as examples, but Anakin Skywalker and Thanos. Skywalker wanted to save his love from death, and Thanos wanted to set the universe back to a simpler, less chaotic time. Admirable goals, but their motives were odious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","user":"Illuminostro","date":". 09-12-2024, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T21:46:03-07:00","id":1541945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537126#post1537126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there's a bit more to the Sabbat than just being Chaotic-Evil. Like a Ventrue Antitribu on the Path of Honor is likely going to be more Lawful-Evil than Chaotic-Evil. Every Sabbat is going to be evil though, murder, especially murder of regular people, is a pretty major point of their organization. And they're not necessarily hobos, they have their own cities and areas they control.<br /> <br /> Though note that's for older editions. In V5 they absolutely only are chaotic-evil murder-hobos.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which they were intended to be from day one. I, a member of a very small minority, think the move to remove Demi-God elders with frankly stupid powers and odious, horrifically repulsive playstiles for psychopaths was a good decision. Do you really want to go back to supplements where you are passive bystanders to watching gods fight? I don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T20:43:30-07:00","id":1542017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1541945#post1541945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which they were intended to be from day one. I, a member of a very small minority, think the move to remove Demi-God elders with frankly stupid powers and odious, horrifically repulsive playstiles for psychopaths was a good decision. Do you really want to go back to supplements where you are passive bystanders to watching gods fight? I don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>A core concept of VtM is the idea of the Jyhad, and that the players are young vampires, pawns in the machinations of the elders, and those elders are themselves simply the pawns of even more ancient vampires, who themselves are the pawns of Methuselah and Antedluvians. This idea of conspiracy within conspiracy within conspiracy has always been pretty central to the the gameline. That doesn't mean that the players should be sitting there on their thumbs while the ST narrates how cool all of these NPCs are, but the solution is not to get rid of all of the elders and turn the Sabbat into NPC monsters-of-the-week.<br /> <br /> There were many ideas and concepts in early VtM that were later revised and improved on, and I always found the Sabbat to be near the top of the list. I find that the Sabbat, as a group of nothing but nomadic murderers is far less interesting and a significant downgrade, both from the player perspective and the Storyteller perspective, than what we had in Revised and V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T22:01:27-07:00","id":1542020,"title":"","content":"I take the view that methusalehs shouldn't be Superman or Darkseid.<br /> <br /> They should be Palpatine.<br /> <br /> Yes, they are formidable physically but it's the WEBS they weave that will fuck you up. If you get in the same room with them, you have a chance to take them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-13-2024, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T22:09:25-07:00","id":1542023,"title":"","content":"Interesting notion CTPhipps. I might go further that if you are in the same room with potent elders and methuselahs for some reason. It's a good bet that they have strongly tilted the odds into there favor and that they got tools that you haven't considered yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-13-2024, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T22:40:09-07:00","id":1542027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542023#post1542023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting notion CTPhipps. I might go further that if you are in the same room with potent elders and methuselahs for some reason. It's a good bet that they have strongly tilted the odds into there favor and that they got tools that you haven't considered yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true.<br /> <br /> However, I feel like the nature of the world is that elders should not be tanking nuclear weapons like Ravnos or ur-shulgi.<br /> <br /> They should be shadowy puppet masters but vulnerable to a rocket launcher and probably much less. Which is why they shouldn't be in a place with a rocket launcher.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm thinking of the Judge from Season 2 of Buffy, also, as what happens when a Methusaleh wakes up after 1000 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-13-2024, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T23:06:13-07:00","id":1542028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542027#post1542027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very true.<br /> <br /> However, I feel like the nature of the world is that elders should not be tanking nuclear weapons like Ravnos or ur-shulgi.<br /> <br /> They should be shadowy puppet masters but vulnerable to a rocket launcher and probably much less.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/tu-fwehFED4\" target=\"_blank\">Quite.</a> (CW: Simulated violence against ballistics gel and a stand-in for a skeleton)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T00:30:58-07:00","id":1542033,"title":"","content":"The Judge played brilliantly by Brian Thompson was a high light of season 2 of Buffy. I was also surprised by how much a good sense of humor he has about playing such parts and I once saw an interview with him about working on Cobra and you learn that he takes the craft pretty seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-13-2024, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T19:27:10-07:00","id":1542084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542020#post1542020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take the view that methusalehs shouldn't be Superman or Darkseid.<br /> <br /> They should be Palpatine.<br /> <br /> Yes, they are formidable physically but it's the WEBS they weave that will fuck you up. If you get in the same room with them, you have a chance to take them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily have a problem with the idea that methuselah, especially eldritch blood gods, are simply beyond the capability of the players to kill under typical circumstances. Like yeah, with some centuries old elder, if you get him alone in a room you can whip out a shotgun and call it a day. But for a methuselah you're going to need to spend a number of sessions planning things out, setting up the plan to deal with them, and you'll likely need some sort of McGuffin or plot device to kill them off. To some degree, ancients like that are themselves plot devices.<br /> <br /> At the same time, those guys generally shouldn't be putting in appearances in the average chronicle anyway, so if one does show up they (and their possible death at the hands of the PCs) should be a major focus of the storyline. Like, look at Bloodlines where just the idea that <i>maybe</i> this old sarcophagus could, possibly, contain some ancient blood god was enough to cause the entire city to implode.<br /> <br /> The issue with VtM's metaplot, for me, was that it started focusing too much on the actions of millennia old ancients and antediluvians, and those are things that should have largely remained in the background rather than being put front and center and especially front and center in a story module (like To Grandmother's House) where PCs basically sit around and watch the NPCs do everything. I think that module in and of itself summarizes everything that was problematic with the WoD at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T21:02:10-07:00","id":1542089,"title":"","content":"I agree with the idea that ancient 4th-6th generation kindred should be very reclusive and the moves they make are more far reaching then the lesser members of the 7th-11th generation who should be the most active players of Kindred society.<br /> <br /> It should be a very rare occasion that you should encounter anyone from the 4th-6th generation and that's how we play it our game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T21:32:56-07:00","id":1542090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542089#post1542089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the idea that ancient 4th-6th generation kindred should be very reclusive and the moves they make are more far reaching then the lesser members of the 7th-11th generation who should be the most active players of Kindred society.<br /> <br /> It should be a very rare occasion that you should encounter anyone from the 4th-6th generation and that's how we play it our game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that when people like Ur-Shulgi do show up, you've essentially made them lesser because having him just personally smiting people and acting like a tank then you diminish what they're supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Their mystery is popped.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like making them indestructible also kind of undermines them because they don't have to be smart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T21:56:26-07:00","id":1542093,"title":"","content":"The first rule of Banu Haqim is that we don't talk about Ur-Shugi at all. That is one character that has outlived it's usefulness, but then he was meant to be a disposable character to serve as a catalyst for the 3rd generation were becoming active again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T22:42:11-07:00","id":1542098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542093#post1542093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first rule of Banu Haqim is that we don't talk about Ur-Shugi at all. That is one character that has outlived it's usefulness, but then he was meant to be a disposable character to serve as a catalyst for the 3rd generation were becoming active again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was hoping he'd get blasted out of existence by the Second Inquisition with air strikes.<br /> <br /> Instead, he's back in the latest supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T23:37:07-07:00","id":1542099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542090#post1542090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more that when people like Ur-Shulgi do show up, you've essentially made them lesser because having him just personally smiting people and acting like a tank then you diminish what they're supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Their mystery is popped.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like making them indestructible also kind of undermines them because they don't have to be smart.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this, I think the new GEHENNA WAR book had It right: yes, you have tour guidelines for statting eldritch monsters, but the 7 Methuselahs are not stat blocks, they are presented as plot hooks. It's their machinations that are interesting for the stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T03:13:00-07:00","id":1542102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542098#post1542098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I was hoping he'd get blasted out of existence by the Second Inquisition with air strikes.<br /> <br /> Instead, he's back in the latest supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really unfortunate. It would have been interesting if he was dead. You basically had a civil war and half the clan left. The survivors were the ones loyal to Ur-Shulgi. If he's suddenly dead then there's a lot of story hooks.<br /> <br /> Hell, maybe he really is dead and his supporters are simply trying to give the appearance that Ur-Shulgi is still alive and leading them because without him their entire sect, or what's left of it, along with their power base will implode.<br /> <br /> And, of course, you can have the Followers of Set or Baali or other traditional enemies of the Assamites sniffing around looking for weaknesses and trying to find the truth of what happened.<br /> <br /> I mine V5 for ideas for my V20 game. Not sure if I'd ever use it but having Ur-Shulgi deader than dead is something I might do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-14-2024, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T05:22:44-07:00","id":1542106,"title":"","content":"IMO Ur-Shulgi is incredably boring as an NPC, I'm bored even of thinking on him. He actually highlight the actual issue of Elders and methusulahs in the game-a lot of time they're just badly written and it's an issue of execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T05:27:07-07:00","id":1542108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542106#post1542106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO Ur-Shulgi is incredably boring as an NPC, I'm bored even of thinking on him. He actually highlight the actual issue of Elders and methusulahs in the game-a lot of time they're just badly written and it's an issue of execution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind him as a plot mover but the question is....what plot.<br /> <br /> He's actually WORSE than introducing Vecna or Sauron into your game because, in fact you can do something about Vecna or Sauron.<br /> <br /> In D&amp;D, you can level grind until you can kill Vecna or you can find the Ring to undo Sauron.<br /> <br /> What does Ur-Shulgi contribute?<br /> <br /> What are the PCs expected to &quot;do&quot; about him?<br /> <br /> Seriously, you can have a big epic campaign to put Cthulhu back to sleep. Ur-Shulgi just IS so you need a super NPC to kill him if you want to get rid of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T05:32:40-07:00","id":1542110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542108#post1542108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't mind him as a plot mover but the question is....what plot.<br /> <br /> He's actually WORSE than introducing Vecna or Sauron into your game because, in fact you can do something about Vecna or Sauron.<br /> <br /> In D&amp;D, you can level grind until you can kill Vecna or you can find the Ring to undo Sauron.<br /> <br /> What does Ur-Shulgi contribute?<br /> <br /> What are the PCs expected to &quot;do&quot; about him?<br /> <br /> Seriously, you can have a big epic campaign to put Cthulhu back to sleep. Ur-Shulgi just IS so you need a super NPC to kill him if you want to get rid of him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The easiest way to see the little goblin of was if he got carpet bombed or somesuch or his though pattern is so alien and ancient you hit it with something It simply wouldn't consider like a simple explosive incendiary device. Go one further and have a coterie of heroic but unamed anarchs do it to emphasize the importance of pc's in the game for once","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T11:25:40-07:00","id":1542122,"title":"","content":"While I'm loath to throw away ANOTHER old NPC from WoD's past, just to remove him from play (we've had enough of that at V5's start), I kind of agree that Ur-Shulgi represents a difficult tool to work with. He's either active enough personally as to be a disruptive element to the game (because it's difficult as hell for the PCs to do anything about him), or he's a puppet master working in the shadows to lead the Web of Knives.<br /> <br /> Let's be clear here: the Web of Knives is the actual gas in the tank of the Assamite schism. Murderous, diablerist religious zealots who follow a twisted vision of their Antedeluvian's will, following the word of a creepy Methuselah who may or may not be a Baali in disguise. THAT'S where the action is. The Web of Knives are what the PCs will encounter most often in campaigns.<br /> <br /> And we don't really need Ur-Shulgi in the picture anymore. The Web of Knives can operate perfectly well in his absence. If you need a Big Bad member of the cult who can menace the Coterie and act as puppetmaster, you can just introduce another, younger Assamite Methuselah who seeks to carry on (what they perceive to be) Ur-Shulgi's/Haqim's plans.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter what the truth is at the heart of a faction's plans. Whether they're right or wrong, backed by a powerful character or not. For normal campaigns, all that matters is what the belief inspires the faction to do.<br /> <br /> (It's the same with the Giovanni. Would the plan to rip down the veil between the Quick and the Dead actually make Clan Giovanni the lords of death? Or would it kill them all? Doesn't matter. Most games will never get that far. All that matters is it's a reason for the Giovanni to be amassing temporal and necromantic power. Ideally, the PCs never let them get that far.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T15:08:06-07:00","id":1542138,"title":"","content":"I think the Web of Knives is a good enemy but kind of redundant with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The irony being the Sabbat is SO MANY THINGS that it actually intrudes on other sects themes.<br /> <br /> They're the occult anarchist terrorist religious fanatic dialberist scheming sect of elders<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T19:55:17-07:00","id":1542162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542138#post1542138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Web of Knives is a good enemy but kind of redundant with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The irony being the Sabbat is SO MANY THINGS that it actually intrudes on other sects themes.<br /> <br /> They're the occult anarchist terrorist religious fanatic dialberist scheming sect of elders</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the issue with the Assamites as that they were always the most difficult independent clan to use. Ur-Shulgi as a plot device to split the clan and get a chunk of them (the part that's easier to use in a game) and add them to the Camarilla is fantastic. But then you're left with the Web of Knives, which essentially just concentrates all of the most problematic aspects of the clan. <br /> <br /> Personally I've never really found much use for the Web of Knives aspect of the clan in my games. If I want a group of diablarists, there are other groups I can use that feel like they will work within the typical VtM plot a lot better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T06:17:22-07:00","id":1542169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Multiple folks</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stuff about ur-Shulgi and the BH.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ur-Shulgi rising, saying &quot;what the fuck happened to this clan, to hell with this Johnny-come-lately Islam shit and fuck the Tremere in particular&quot;, and tearing the clan a new asshole is ultimately an interesting concept that was overall positive for the clan's depiction. It even being one of the first Baali is even good. However, I do feel in retrospect it would have been more interesting and thematically richer to have taken it one of two ways:<br /> <br /> 1. Ur-Shulgi rose and led the schism personally, as opposed to al-Ashrad. Then you've got the question of why is a potential Baali &quot;infiltrator&quot; leading his own caste to the Camarilla, and what role in the Jyhad it plays. And by implication, maybe Haqim <i>did</i> rise from torpor in the 7th Century, convert to Islam, and direct his clan to convert and join/found the Ashirra after all as some BH claim. Then, you've got a reason for the Web of Knives to target the Camarilla -- they're acting on Haqim's orders to wage a Third Baali War as a shadow theater of the Gehenna War itself.<br /> <br /> 2. Things play out as canon, except instead of the Web being a degenerate, Methuselah-worshipping, opportunistic hunter Gehenna cult...they take the discretion, secrecy, and surgical precision for which the BH had been previously known to the extreme. They follow Haqim's mandate -- and Noddist proclamation -- to the letter and spirit to a fault: they respect no domain, they honor no hospitality, they hold accounting in perpetuity, and they consider the right to destruction their sole and exclusive privilege. Vampires deemed &quot;unworthy&quot; just...disappear, irrespective of age, generation, clan, sect, status, or title. And, no one quite knows <i>why</i>, or by what metric they're being judged -- in fact, the only reason anyone would believe it's the Web (or even be aware of its existence) is down to the schismatics' word.<br /> <br /> It'd be even more interesting if they were specifically hunting ancillae and elders who resist the Beckoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T08:17:23-07:00","id":1542175,"title":"","content":"That's a good question of how do you use Ur-Shugi in any capacity as he is a wrecking ball to the setting and was used as a plot device for a game line that was going to be ending.<br /> <br /> Now with Gehenna retooled and there world didn't end the way they thought. Of what use is he now as he only meant to be a disposable character and giving him a personality wasn't a big deal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T08:42:51-07:00","id":1542177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542175#post1542175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good question of how do you use Ur-Shugi in any capacity as he is a wrecking ball to the setting and was used as a plot device for a game line that was going to be ending.<br /> <br /> Now with Gehenna retooled and there world didn't end the way they thought. Of what use is he now as he only meant to be a disposable character and giving him a personality wasn't a big deal?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's always been useful in my games as a Worf figure.<br /> <br /> 1. Tremere/Saulot destroyed him to show how powerful he was.<br /> <br /> 2. He got blowed up by the US military to show how the Second Inquisition was not to be fucked with.<br /> <br /> 3. The PCs once bound him with a true magic scroll that thwarted Gehenna for awhile.<br /> <br /> 4. A repowered Mithras gathered a group of his fellow Methuselahs to destroy him.<br /> <br /> 5. He once got swallowed by Haqim's blood.<br /> <br /> Yeah...I may have issues with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T09:01:38-07:00","id":1542180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537437#post1537437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have of a lot of interesting stories and ideas for how to do the V5 Sabbat but it occurs to me that Paradox was never interested in explaining it so why should I have spent so much time thinking through.<br /> <br /> I am, however, interested in the Storyteller's Vault SABBAT: SCHISMS that's coming out at the end of the month. The premise for that being the Sabbat is actually split in two with the Gehenna Crusaders being essentially the mobile army of crazy people.<br /> <br /> I think the reason the Sabbat abandoned all of their territory was the Out of Universe reason that they didn't want huge chunks of the Central and South American player base to be denied Camarilla games in their hometowns. Not getting, I suspect, that most people worked around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as a Brazilian I have to say that in my games, Brazil, just like all the rest, is contested territory, some are Sabbath, some cities are Cammy. It's actually a pretty simple headcanon to do, and everybody around here that I know that plays the game do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T09:07:21-07:00","id":1542183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1537456#post1537456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, I wouldn't even necessarily mind that. The Beckoning is supposed to be a big thing, most of the Elders have gone to the Middle East both the Camarilla's Elders and (in theory) the Sabbat's Elders, and it would make sense that more Sabbat members would head over there than Camarilla members. Many would get dragged along because of their vinculum ties, or simply because killing Elder vampires in the Gehenna Crusade is kind of a big thing that the Sabbat does. It's not hard to imagine that a lot of them would say, &quot;Gehenna is here! Our time has come!&quot; and head off to fight. Personally I intensely dislike the idea of the Beckoning, but this is stuff that makes sense given the context of V5.<br /> <br /> But then the books never did anything else with the Beckoning, due to the fact that it's such a massive world-shaking piece of metaplot that any sort of examination of it is going to take the focus off of the street-level stories that V5 wants players to prioritize. And then apparently Justin is suggesting that the Sabbat elders weren't really affected by the Beckoning and didn't join in the Gehenna War. They're actually still around, and still in charge of the Sabbat, it's just that they decided to implode their own sect and destroy everything they've spent centuries building for reasons - even though the Beckoning and Gehenna War are a pretty solid explanation as to why Sabbat Elders wouldn't be around why the sect would collapse without them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the same mistake they made in Rev MtA with the Avatar Storm and the blown of the Masters... It seems they didn't learn their lessons after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T09:12:41-07:00","id":1542184,"title":"","content":"Omg the Worf factor<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. That brings back memories of how Worf was this bad ass Klingon warrior, but got beaten up so badly that it became a running gag.<br /> <br /> When a possessed Counselor Troi breaks your wrist with ease and your out of the game. Maybe it's time to change careers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T10:33:10-07:00","id":1542186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542175#post1542175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good question of how do you use Ur-Shugi in any capacity as he is a wrecking ball to the setting and was used as a plot device for a game line that was going to be ending.<br /> <br /> Now with Gehenna retooled and there world didn't end the way they thought. Of what use is he now as he only meant to be a disposable character and giving him a personality wasn't a big deal?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same could be said for any methuselah, frankly. Methuselahs exist on a level never really intended for players to interact with over the course of normal chronicles, or frankly for their schemes to have any immediate influence over the scope of a single chronicle. But at the same time, every ST, their players, and their cats want to run that epic chronicle where either the PC's are that truly special, what they're doing is so integral to the Jyhad, or at the perfect confluence of multiple methuselahs' schemes, they can't help but show up. Usually, when they're less-experienced with the game and don't really have a feel for the scope or scale of the setting.<br /> <br /> Granted, White Wolf writing city and premade chronicle books with methuselahs fucking about like idiots hasn't helped.<br /> <br /> Your average methuselah couldn't give a shit if the Sheriff of Cleveland is plotting against their Prince, let alone that Sheriff has bamboozled some dipshit neonates into acting in service to those plots. Your average methuselah couldn't give a shit if there is a Prince of Cleveland, or who. Your average methuselah couldn't give a shit Cleveland's Camarilla. Your average methuselah likely barely gives a shit Cleveland even exists. That's their elder pawns' jobs, and their pawns' pawns' jobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T11:31:48-07:00","id":1542188,"title":"","content":"Your right that most ancients wouldn't really be concerned by the happenings of what is going in Chicago, New York, Toronto or Vancouver unless they reside there. Sometimes I found it hard to picture that even elders that Moncada would concern himself of what is going in the New World when he would have enough to deal with Madrid as he is more or less the Prince there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T12:02:52-07:00","id":1542192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542177#post1542177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's always been useful in my games as a Worf figure.<br /> <br /> 1. Tremere/Saulot destroyed him to show how powerful he was.<br /> <br /> 2. He got blowed up by the US military to show how the Second Inquisition was not to be fucked with.<br /> <br /> 3. The PCs once bound him with a true magic scroll that thwarted Gehenna for awhile.<br /> <br /> 4. A repowered Mithras gathered a group of his fellow Methuselahs to destroy him.<br /> <br /> 5. He once got swallowed by Haqim's blood.<br /> <br /> Yeah...I may have issues with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>No more then most people on this forum. Though I got a visual of Haqim being a parent coming to your haven and asking if Ur-Shugi is there and it's past his bedtime. \ud83d\ude03<br /> <br /> And the Sheperd is crashing on your couch reading Manga or coloring or playing video games .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-15-2024, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T12:09:37-07:00","id":1542193,"title":"","content":"Portia was notably the exception because even in 1st Edition, that was a fun idea.<br /> <br /> Mind you, my players always sided with her over Menele because she was hot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T12:52:53-07:00","id":1542194,"title":"","content":"The hotness adds a major advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T12:53:54-07:00","id":1542195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542188#post1542188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your right that most ancients wouldn't really be concerned by the happenings of what is going in Chicago, New York, Toronto or Vancouver unless they reside there. Sometimes I found it hard to picture that even elders that Moncada would concern himself of what is going in the New World when he would have enough to deal with Madrid as he is more or less the Prince there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much geographical concerns in my mind, as it is methuselahs -- <i>true</i> methuselahs -- have been there and done that for pretty much anything, and temporal politics -- mortal or vampire -- are just not on their radar.<br /> <br /> I mean, I should take a step back on that one and work with some definitions. A methuselah is technically any vampire more than a thousand years old, generally of the fourth and fifth generations but some sixth or even seventh generation vampires should certainly be attributed with the label. But, there's still a huge difference between a vampire embraced in the wake of the collapse of the Roman empire, and those embraced prior to the <i>rise</i> of it, or in some cases the Bronze Age collapse or even the dawn of human civilization...even among vampires of the same nominal generation.<br /> <br /> You rightly pointed out the &quot;discovery&quot; of the Americas as something of which methuselahs may not take interest, but it's in far excess of that. These are vampires that have seen wars that last centuries, the rise and fall of empires and dynasties that lasted a thousand years and spanned the world as it was &quot;known&quot; at the time, <i>multiple</i> &quot;ends of the world&quot; and consequent dark ages. If you witnessed -- hell, actively participated in or helped cause -- an event like the Bronze Age collapse, the threat of nuclear holocaust just won't hit the same. If anything, a methuselah that old will likely just laugh and say the sooner, the better. At least it would wipe the planet of excess human populations and all this problematic technology, and bring back &quot;the good old days&quot;.<br /> <br /> Even among vampire politics...Camarilla, Sabbat? they're fads, just two new factions of, by, and for no-account inferiors to elevate their own station, waging the same conflicts that have <i>always</i> been waged between vampires. The Ashirra predates either by nearly a millennium, and even <i>that's</i> a &quot;new&quot; sect based entirely around -- of all things -- a <i>mortal</i> religion. They're nothing compared to the Second City, Carthage and Rome, and whatever vampiric societies lost to time existed in between. And just like those, these new sects will pass into history in time -- and so will their celebrants and apologists, unless they wise up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T13:00:55-07:00","id":1542197,"title":"","content":"My definition of ancients are over 2,000+ and usually are around the 4th-6th generation and the ones that are 1,000 years old are still elders and haven't go through the profound emotional and mental changes that true ancients have gone through yet.<br /> <br /> But to be fair, that is how we do it our game that the most active elders are members of the 7th-9th generation with the 10th and 11th generations starting to come into there power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-15-2024, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T16:14:12-07:00","id":1542206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542169#post1542169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. Things play out as canon, except instead of the Web being a degenerate, Methuselah-worshipping, opportunistic hunter Gehenna cult...they take the discretion, secrecy, and surgical precision for which the BH had been previously known to the extreme. They follow Haqim's mandate -- and Noddist proclamation -- to the letter and spirit to a fault: they respect no domain, they honor no hospitality, they hold accounting in perpetuity, and they consider the right to destruction their sole and exclusive privilege. Vampires deemed &quot;unworthy&quot; just...disappear, irrespective of age, generation, clan, sect, status, or title. And, no one quite knows <i>why</i>, or by what metric they're being judged -- in fact, the only reason anyone would believe it's the Web (or even be aware of its existence) is down to the schismatics' word.<br /> <br /> It'd be even more interesting if they were specifically hunting ancillae and elders who resist the Beckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you describe could, in fact, BE the Beckoning, misunderstood as elders being drawn abroad to fight on behalf of their sires when they're really being quietly assassinated, some after making noises about/preparations for getting out of Dodge in reaction to the first disappearances. Of course there'd need to be an explanation for why the Hecata aren't being targeted.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T19:33:04-07:00","id":1542215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542206#post1542206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you describe could, in fact, BE the Beckoning, misunderstood as elders being drawn abroad to fight on behalf of their sires when they're really being quietly assassinated, some after making noises about/preparations for getting out of Dodge in reaction to the first disappearances. Of course there'd need to be an explanation for why the Hecata aren't being targeted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As I understood it, one of the few in-universe theories about the Beckoning was it was just Ur-Shulgi and the Methusalehs opposed to him summoning vampires to the Middle East to fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T19:51:50-07:00","id":1542216,"title":"","content":"That's a good theory that the Beckoning is simply 4th-6th generation ancients having a conflict and are drawing in there chosen pawns to serve them. Or they are themselves are acting at the behest of the 3rd generation who want to cull there respective lineages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T03:17:58-07:00","id":1542239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542197#post1542197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My definition of ancients are over 2,000+ and usually are around the 4th-6th generation and the ones that are 1,000 years old are still elders and haven't go through the profound emotional and mental changes that true ancients have gone through yet.<br /> <br /> But to be fair, that is how we do it our game that the most active elders are members of the 7th-9th generation with the 10th and 11th generations starting to come into there power.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is (indirectly) one of the reasons I prefer the concept of Gehenna as cyclical, and merely a supernatural event correspondent to regional, continental, or global crises if not outright civilizational collapse. There's a mass die-off among neonates and ancillae, elders close ranks or die off, methuselahs start calling audibles in response to rapid upheaval, maybe an Antediluvian rolls over and farts in their sleep; at the end, vampires repopulate and occupy new social niches as best-fits however mortal society reshapes itself, in accordance to whatever vampiric sects rise out of the ashes. Either way generations consolidate, and &quot;age gaps&quot; manifest between the vampires who survived the events and those embraced in their wake.<br /> <br /> From there you can categorize and sub-categorize vampires by how many &quot;apocalypses&quot; a vampire survived, and the psychological impact of each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T09:50:25-07:00","id":1542251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542194#post1542194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hotness adds a major advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be a damned shame if super hottie Ancient was...a Nosferatu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T11:47:19-07:00","id":1542260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542251#post1542251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Be a damned shame if super hottie Ancient was...a Nosferatu</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done a few Eberron games where the protagonist's girlfriend was a Hag. He doesn't care as beauty is only...<br /> <br /> *puts on sunglasses*<br /> <br /> Skin deep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T12:50:49-07:00","id":1542264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542260#post1542260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've done a few Eberron games where the protagonist's girlfriend was a Hag. He doesn't care as beauty is only...<br /> <br /> *puts on sunglasses*<br /> <br /> Skin deep.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Im here to kick ass and chew bubblegum.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T14:30:20-07:00","id":1542271,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sadly we ran out of bubblegum at the store. But take these toy cars as a bonus gift.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T18:16:25-07:00","id":1542280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542177#post1542177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's always been useful in my games as a Worf figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically the only use I can find for him.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m unconvinced that he was even needed for the Schism, the tension between the two factions could have been solved another way with the same effect. And even granting that point, the possibility of his coming awakening was far more relevant for the Schism than the actual happenstance.<br /> <br /> The Web of Knives is by itself unnecessary baggage, too. Not only does it fills a niche that\u2019s kinda cluttered already, Ur-Shulgi removed the only thing that made them unique. All the Web did was keep the problematic aspects of the clan still existing.<br /> <br /> My opinion persist that the best way to show the power of the Second Inquisition in V5 would have been to bombard the Allamut instead of the Vienna Chantry. Cleaner, more sensible, it would greatly impress the vampires all the same, and we wouldn\u2019t lose anything of real value to the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542186#post1542186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same could be said for any methuselah, frankly. Methuselahs exist on a level never really intended for players to interact with over the course of normal chronicles</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, if not greatly.<br /> <br /> Methuselahs are characters. However you see them as humane or not, they can fill a lot of narrative niches.<br /> <br /> Decently written methuselah can fill niches that don\u2019t relate to direct confrontation. They may have plans and minions that carry some sort of narrative signature, they may be shadows looming in the distance that have some color and personality to them, they may even once in a while interact with the characters.<br /> <br /> Lair of the Hidden is a prime example, if not the most popular scenario around, of how you can have a whole story with the PCs interacting with Methuselahs without any need for them to ever try to do harm to those ancient vampires.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi\u2019s greatest crime isn\u2019t that he is too powerful. It\u2019s that he is too boring. The guy is a freaking Villain Sue with less personality than a spoon. He comes to change the status-quo with his pinky and then just sits there being invincible.<br /> <br /> And it is important to make it clear: Methuselahs aren\u2019t invincible. While they can\u2019t be beaten by the PCs, the narrative is all about how they constantly maneuver against each other, So there are theoretical limits to what they can and will do. Ur-Shulgi simply doesn\u2019t care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T18:44:57-07:00","id":1542283,"title":"","content":"At this point. I don't think that even a great creative talent like a Grant Morrison could do much with Ur-Shugi as how do you depict what is more or less a child that sees things in stark simple terms and no nuances?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T03:31:52-07:00","id":1542303,"title":"","content":"The Web of Knives being a bunch of diablerist religious fanatics as a problematic element reminds me of the question of how much you modify a bad concept before it's not even related to the original idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T08:26:25-07:00","id":1542314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542280#post1542280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, if not greatly.<br /> <br /> Methuselahs are characters. However you see them as humane or not, they can fill a lot of narrative niches.<br /> <br /> Decently written methuselah can fill niches that don\u2019t relate to direct confrontation. They may have plans and minions that carry some sort of narrative signature, they may be shadows looming in the distance that have some color and personality to them, they may even once in a while interact with the characters.<br /> <br /> Lair of the Hidden is a prime example, if not the most popular scenario around, of how you can have a whole story with the PCs interacting with Methuselahs without any need for them to ever try to do harm to those ancient vampires.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi\u2019s greatest crime isn\u2019t that he is too powerful. It\u2019s that he is too boring. The guy is a freaking Villain Sue with less personality than a spoon. He comes to change the status-quo with his pinky and then just sits there being invincible.<br /> <br /> And it is important to make it clear: Methuselahs aren\u2019t invincible. While they can\u2019t be beaten by the PCs, the narrative is all about how they constantly maneuver against each other, So there are theoretical limits to what they can and will do. Ur-Shulgi simply doesn\u2019t care.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that so much as it is a matter of scale. Real-world comparison time, let's look at Amazon and imagine what it might look like as a vampire clan. It's stupid, but it'll work.<br /> <br /> Bezos is the Amazon Antediluvian. He fucked off and is doing what-the-fuck-ever with his entertainment reporter ghoul, on his penis rockets and half-billion-dollar waterborne doomsday bunker. HIs only interest nowadays is how quickly he can divest from his own clan to raise up the Blue Origin bloodline in its wake without getting put on the Red List by the Securities Exchange Commission sect for Insider Gehenna Preparation.<br /> <br /> The Amazon clan's C-suite are its methuselahs. Their job is making sure the Amazon clan's elders, ancilla, and neonates are the yummiest available, packing every precious drop of blood with the highest-value vitae, delivered quarterly to all the outside vampires who just can't help their regular snack attacks. They don't give a hot, wet, stinking shit what happens in any individual region, division, warehouse, or headquarters on a daily, weekly, quarterly, or annual basis so long as the rivers of vitae flow. And as such, their only concern is the overall flow of business as usual, directing it here and there to ensure the middle management stays on track and in line.<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, they're the ones who run the Amazon clan. They adhere to their Antediluvian's will and &quot;vision&quot;, but within the constraints of clan they're the power brokers. In exchange for that temporal power, they're also the Antediluvian's favored scapegoats, and when the unsustainable monolith inevitably comes crashing down -- and it will, sooner or later, not from within but without -- they'll be the ones getting eaten while their Antediluvian ejaculates himself into space.<br /> <br /> The middle management are the elders and ancillae. Their job is to keep those rivers of vitae flowing so the C-suite stays happy, <i>they're</i> the ones whose job is all that &quot;small-scale&quot; bullshit.<br /> <br /> Everybody else? fuck 'em. Neonates might be unhappy and there's a constant undercurrent of another Anarch revolt against the clan, but again, that's the elders' and ancillaes' job to bust up. The clan is structured in a way to ensure neonates are constantly at each other's throats, and no neonate survives long enough to start organizing the others anyways. Christophus Smallus might've accidentally gotten a methuselah tagged, but ultimately it was that methuselah's fault for saying a bunch of dumb racist shit on a platform he didn't fully understand, and giving the other methuselahs an excuse to diablerize him &quot;for the good of the clan&quot; under the table.<br /> <br /> ...is Jeff Bezos Saulot in disguise? who fucking knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-17-2024, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T22:19:24-07:00","id":1542414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1542314#post1542314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that so much as it is a matter of scale. Real-world comparison time, let's look at Amazon and imagine what it might look like as a vampire clan. It's stupid, but it'll work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like they need to start up some kind of union or something. In fact, I think you've just given me the idea for my next Ventrue Anarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T17:08:56-07:00","id":1543602,"title":"","content":"Good luck with that AnubisXy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T05:41:15-07:00","id":1543746,"title":"","content":"Ur-Shulgi has to be vague and unseen to be effective, I think.<br /> <br /> In V20, I think he was merely &quot;stirring&quot;, rather than actually awake. That wasn't a bad idea. Once he's awake, that's when it becomes a huge problem\u2014because, realistically, he would act, and the result would be devastating.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think you <i>have</i> to kill him, but you <i>do</i> have to play up the doubt if you don't. He's allegedly awake, but isn't doing anything, so there has to be a plausible reason for why that is.<br /> <br /> Is he in a fugue state and unable to act? Is he wandering the Earth to find his lost sire? Is he trapped between worlds? Did he sacrifice himself to remove the Tremere Curse? Or maybe he used Daimonion 9 and is now just some cosmic horror with alien drives and plans?<br /> <br /> Or maybe he's just a ruse by elders with high-level Obfuscate? Or maybe it's not really Ur-Shulgi at all, but one of the Aralu/Children? Or maybe he just woke up, did a Ravnos, and got blasted back to whatever Hell he crawled out of? (Cue the Week of Nightmares, Mk. II, but targeting the Web of Knives. Probably an unpopular thing to do setting-wide, but it would be fun for individual tables.)<br /> <br /> What if Alamut was actually built on the original Well of Sacrifice? Maybe that's why the Schismatics have left. They know something awful is forming down there, from whatever remained of Ur-Shulgi's soul.<br /> <br /> Who really threw off the Tremere Curse? Or could the clan always have opted out (like the antitribu did)? Maybe it was actually just Tremere losing his body that ended the curse? In which case, Ur-Shulgi might never have been involved at all.<br /> <br /> If the Aapilu are a thing now, maybe all that congealed vitae the Banu Haqim have been gathering at Alamut has just gained sentience and become a nightmare spirit of blood? Heck, it could even be Ur-Shulgi (or an echo of him), albeit without a body. Maybe that's why he can't act yet? But people can imbibe portions of him to perform incredible magic\u2014such as breaking the Tremere Curse.<br /> <br /> But nearly all of these ideas hinge on Ur-Shulgi being a concept and not really an active entity that poses a wider threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T10:35:51-07:00","id":1543887,"title":"","content":"Really good analysis there <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a>, regarding Methuselahs as story hooks rather than immovable obstacles. Not for nothing, my favorite Methuselah is <b>Sybil </b>and we can count the facts we &quot;know&quot; about her one one hand. She's (Lasombra)'s only direct female childe, she's Marcus Vitel's sire, she's manipulated the North American Tremere for centuries, and she wants to use the United States nuclear arsenal to <i>nuke the Antediluvian's.</i><br /> <br /> This kinda parallels a conversation I'm having on reddit about how the &quot;Content treadmill&quot; of White Wolf (and the RPG industry in general) during the 90's seems to suffer from the same problems as late-stage MCU. Each new product is mostly concerned with (a) dropping easter-eggs for previous/upcoming projects or (b) setting up the next &quot;episode&quot; (weather it be a movie or a streaming show) to the detriment of the plot of the movie or show you are currently watching.<br /> <br /> The reveal of Ur-Shulgi in <i>Children of the Night</i> suffers from the same issues. His entire entry is an easter-egg hunt or an additional puzzle piece of the Salout/Baali/Haquim clusterfuck. Its written in an impenetrable and mythological style. Which, hey, you get points for adhering to a theme and mood. And I appreciate the compliment to my intelligence that I'm supposed to infer all these great stories that could be told using this character but a bit of plain text like @adambeyoncelow laid out above about how you could use not only his emergence but RUMORS of his emergence to motivate actions in your story.<br /> <br /> Since this tread is already massively off topic I may start another thread asking folks to do just that with their favorite Methuselahs. Weirdly, for one who's opinions on the V5 plot are rarely positive, I think that V5 has managed to do this right at least once with the Master of Ravens. No one is quite sure who he is or even what clan he is from. His powers and abilities are not nearly as important as the uproar he causes and the affect he has on younger kindred social movements. The fact the Inner Circle was vetoed from making him Anathema is a great plot hook as long as we don't know who issued the veto.<br /> <br /> And, dang, the more I think of <i>Children of the Night</i> the more I see the MCU parallels. CotN gives us some mysterious and evocative Inconnu members, the various Monitors. Seemed like we were finally getting some breadcumbs about the most secretive of Sects. What we finally get in Lair of the Hidden is a letdown on par with what Secret Invasion accomplished with the fantastic set up it had been given. Jalan/Karsh is just another easter egg hunt. But I digress...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T12:04:45-07:00","id":1543900,"title":"","content":"Oddly outside of the Setite ancient Qurem Hera from Children Of The Night or Dracon from the Tzismce, I don't have a favorite ancient in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T17:25:24-07:00","id":1543932,"title":"","content":"You know that I do like Polina of the American Sabbat, I like that he described being a smart and capable tactical expert that doesn't let his pride get in the way to often and he shocked his clan that he survived his embrace and gained incredible intelligence on the lupines and gained greater potency through amaranth. I also was struck that his most treasured item is an antique silver cross that his long dead mother gave him and still means a great deal to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T02:33:53-07:00","id":1544188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcusVitel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs?p=1543887#post1543887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really good analysis there <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a>, regarding Methuselahs as story hooks rather than immovable obstacles. Not for nothing, my favorite Methuselah is <b>Sybil </b>and we can count the facts we &quot;know&quot; about her one one hand. She's (Lasombra)'s only direct female childe, she's Marcus Vitel's sire, she's manipulated the North American Tremere for centuries, and she wants to use the United States nuclear arsenal to <i>nuke the Antediluvian's.</i><br /> <br /> This kinda parallels a conversation I'm having on reddit about how the &quot;Content treadmill&quot; of White Wolf (and the RPG industry in general) during the 90's seems to suffer from the same problems as late-stage MCU. Each new product is mostly concerned with (a) dropping easter-eggs for previous/upcoming projects or (b) setting up the next &quot;episode&quot; (weather it be a movie or a streaming show) to the detriment of the plot of the movie or show you are currently watching.<br /> <br /> The reveal of Ur-Shulgi in <i>Children of the Night</i> suffers from the same issues. His entire entry is an easter-egg hunt or an additional puzzle piece of the Salout/Baali/Haquim clusterfuck. Its written in an impenetrable and mythological style. Which, hey, you get points for adhering to a theme and mood. And I appreciate the compliment to my intelligence that I'm supposed to infer all these great stories that could be told using this character but a bit of plain text like @adambeyoncelow laid out above about how you could use not only his emergence but RUMORS of his emergence to motivate actions in your story.<br /> <br /> Since this tread is already massively off topic I may start another thread asking folks to do just that with their favorite Methuselahs. Weirdly, for one who's opinions on the V5 plot are rarely positive, I think that V5 has managed to do this right at least once with the Master of Ravens. No one is quite sure who he is or even what clan he is from. His powers and abilities are not nearly as important as the uproar he causes and the affect he has on younger kindred social movements. The fact the Inner Circle was vetoed from making him Anathema is a great plot hook as long as we don't know who issued the veto.<br /> <br /> And, dang, the more I think of <i>Children of the Night</i> the more I see the MCU parallels. CotN gives us some mysterious and evocative Inconnu members, the various Monitors. Seemed like we were finally getting some breadcumbs about the most secretive of Sects. What we finally get in Lair of the Hidden is a letdown on par with what Secret Invasion accomplished with the fantastic set up it had been given. Jalan/Karsh is just another easter egg hunt. But I digress...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your kind words! It's a tricky line to walk, for sure. The WoD benefits from the fact that it isn't a novel or movie, so dangling loads of mysteries and setting up things to come is perfectly fine \u2014 but tables need options, not railroads.<br /> <br /> When laying out lots of potentially conflicting information, it's better to treat the metaplot as a guideline rather than the law. But also, when you keep stuff vague, don't backtrack and give it a definite answer later on unless you're prepared for how that will upset the games people have already been playing.<br /> <br /> I think this is something V20 actually does really well. We get all the usual IC &quot;unreliable narrator&quot; stuff, followed by chunks of OOC lore, and then a bunch of bullet points for how this could be explored in a chronicle. Being metaplot agnostic is actually the perfect fit for this type of game, because the point isn't to lay down canon but to provoke creativity.<br /> <br /> People actually end up engaging with more of the metaplot if they have more leeway to make it fit their stories (and there's less risk their games will be invalidated by future supplements).<br /> <br /> The problem comes in, say, Revised or V5 when you say or imply there's a particular story unfolding and that you have a particular set of answers to the great mysteries of the setting which may or may not be revealed. How can you plan ahead in that context if you want to use the metaplot? You can't.<br /> <br /> So it becomes a story you passively consume and you maybe sprinkle a few bits into your story, but it's mostly something that doesn't affect your tables at all. Then you either stop buying the books, or you buy them and feel alienated from the same setting which previously drew you on.<br /> <br /> Think of the Beckoning. It felt like ParaWolf wanted it to be a big mystery, as it's a big part of the setting, but it was unclear if it would ever be answered. So people mostly ignored it, because otherwise, you risk establishing things as facts that would be later contradicted by the books. (And also, dangling a mystery without much development is just kinda boring. Those few suggestions in the Gehenna War supplement should have been there in the CRB's Storytelling chapter.)<br /> <br /> If you have hard points (things that have to happen) and soft points (things that might happen but don't have to or could happen in a different way) in the metaplot, you should signal which is which. Soft points are generally going to be better than hard points, because every hard point is going to risk alienating people or invalidating parts of the setting. When you explain whether they're firm changes or optional suggestions, you should also give some ideas about how they may affect individual games and some options for how to make it fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10-18-2024, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T02:40:26-07:00","id":1544189,"title":"","content":"And I got gobbled by the spam daemon. Oops!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}